    <node id="Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent Authorities are designated regulatory bodies with a multifaceted role in overseeing the compliance and safety standards associated with various regulatory frameworks, particularly in relation to biometric data processing and artificial intelligence (AI). Their primary responsibility is to enforce laws and regulations pertaining to biometric data processing, which includes ensuring compliance with data protection legislation. 

In the realm of AI, Competent Authorities are tasked with supervising the deployment and operation of high-risk AI systems. They hold specific supervisory powers that enable them to oversee testing, monitoring, and adherence to regulatory frameworks at both Union and national levels. These authorities work in close collaboration with the AI Office to ensure compliance with various AI regulations, reflecting their integral role in the governance of AI technologies. This includes managing the implementation of AI projects and enhancing transparency by publishing relevant information on their respective websites.

Competent Authorities play a critical role in ensuring that high-risk AI systems meet appropriate safety and legal standards. They are also responsible for reporting and investigating serious incidents related to AI, which underscores their importance in maintaining accountability and upholding safety standards within the AI landscape. Furthermore, they oversee the application and enforcement of financial regulations, particularly those impacting AI in financial services, guiding entities involved in data processing to navigate compliance requirements appropriately.

Overall, Competent Authorities operate as the cornerstone of regulatory oversight, enforcing compliance and guiding the development and testing of AI systems while ensuring that associated risks are managed effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent Authorities are governmental bodies responsible for overseeing the implementation of regulations and ensuring compliance among market operators.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent Authorities are regulatory bodies tasked with overseeing the implementation and management of AI regulatory sandboxes, ensuring compliance with laws and regulations during the development of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent Authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing the implementation of the regulation and ensuring access to high-quality data for AI training and validation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936291</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement Authorities are governmental bodies tasked with maintaining public order and ensuring public safety. Their primary responsibilities include preventing, investigating, detecting, and prosecuting criminal offenses, which are essential for overall public security. These authorities operate within legal frameworks that govern the processing of personal data, ensuring compliance while performing their duties related to public safety and criminal justice.

As part of their efforts to combat crime, Law Enforcement Authorities often integrate advanced technologies, particularly artificial intelligence (AI) systems. These technologies assist in assessing risks and conducting investigations into criminal activities. They also engage in identity verification and conduct identity checks as part of their law enforcement responsibilities. The deployment of high-risk AI systems, particularly for biometric identification, occurs under specific legal regulations, highlighting the balance between technological advancement and compliance with protective data provisions.

Law Enforcement Authorities encompass a range of organizations responsible for enforcing laws, maintaining public order, and safeguarding national security. While they may utilize high-risk AI systems under certain circumstances, they do so under strict legal frameworks, ensuring both the effectiveness of their operations and the protection of individual rights. Overall, Law Enforcement Authorities play a crucial role in crime prevention and prosecution while adapting to the evolving landscape of technology and law enforcement practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Law Enforcement Authorities utilize AI systems and have specific conformity assessment procedures stipulated in the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement authorities are governmental organizations responsible for maintaining public order and enforcing the law, and they play a critical role in the deployment of biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement authorities are government agencies responsible for maintaining public order and enforcing laws, with specific considerations during the monitoring of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-239d42cf353b4be7fdeade1f3fced85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6badc71855b10bbd17a31c7dfef0c442&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_155.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
