    <node id="Public and Private Entities">
      <data key="d0">Public and Private Entities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Public and private entities are organizations that may develop or utilize AI systems for various purposes, including military and defense.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member States">
      <data key="d0">Member States</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States are countries that are part of the European Union (EU), serving as individual sovereign entities that comprise the larger political and economic union. They play a critical role in the EU's collective governance and regulatory framework, actively participating in the application and enforcement of EU laws and regulations across various sectors, including immigration, human rights, artificial intelligence (AI), medical devices, and law enforcement. 

As integral components of the EU's governance structure, Member States are bound by its treaties and regulations, ensuring compliance with directives through collaboration. They designate representatives to a Board responsible for overseeing discussions on AI regulations, contributing to the implementation and enforcement of AI policies. This cooperative governance allows Member States to engage in dialogues that balance innovation with the protection of workers’ rights and national security.

To support responsible innovation, Member States have established regulatory sandboxes to manage potential risks associated with new technologies. They are also involved in developing codes of conduct for AI systems and must adhere to specified notification processes aligned with relevant regulations. Their commitment to fostering a regulatory framework emphasizes safety, compliance, and innovation.

Additionally, Member States uphold human rights, evidenced by their adherence to the UN Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, which highlights their dedication to social responsibility. In summary, Member States are essential to the EU’s comprehensive regulatory framework, ensuring collective safety, compliance, and progressive innovation across the Union while participating in the legislative processes and enforcement activities outlined by EU provisions and utilizing AI testing support structures.</data>
