    <node id="Article 4(2) TEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 4(2) TEU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 4(2) TEU is a legal provision within the Treaty on European Union that pertains to the responsibilities of Member States regarding national security and defense.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Union Defence Policy">
      <data key="d0">Common Union Defence Policy</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Common Union Defence Policy refers to the collective defense strategies formulated by EU Member States, aimed at cooperation in military and defense activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civilian Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Civilian Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civilian Purposes refer to non-military uses of AI systems that are compliant with regulations, such as law enforcement and humanitarian efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems Regulation">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Systems Regulation refers to laws and guidelines that govern the development, deployment, and use of artificial intelligence technologies, particularly concerning military and security applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Systems Regulation outlines compliance requirements for AI systems, particularly those in large-scale IT systems before specific deadlines.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Systems Regulation establishes transparency obligations for the deployment of AI systems, ensuring compliance with legal standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0044fdddd0a21caecd46a12639588d98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_137.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Military Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Military Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Military Purposes refer to uses of AI systems that are specifically intended for defense, combat, or defense-related operations and activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Security">
      <data key="d0">National Security</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National Security encompasses the strategies and measures taken by a state to protect its citizens, territory, and values from external threats.&lt;SEP&gt;National security encompasses the strategies and measures undertaken by a state to ensure the protection and safety of its citizens and territorial integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public International Law">
      <data key="d0">Public International Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public International Law is a set of legal norms and principles governing the relations between sovereign states which play a significant role in military and defense policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civilian or Humanitarian Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Civilian or Humanitarian Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civilian or Humanitarian Purposes include uses of AI systems for non-combat activities, such as providing aid, law enforcement, or public safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance with Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Compliance with Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance with Regulations involves ensuring that the use and deployment of AI systems meet legal and ethical standards set forth in relevant laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Union Law">
      <data key="d0">European Union Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">European Union Law consists of treaties, regulations, and directives that govern the Member States within the EU, influencing national security and defense policy.&lt;SEP&gt;European Union law provides guidelines and regulations governing the operation and oversight of high-risk AI systems, including requirements for human verification.&lt;SEP&gt;European Union Law sets forth rules and procedures, including the imposition of administrative fines, that Member States must follow.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation refers to a comprehensive legal framework established by the European Union (EU) and its Member States, aimed at governing the development, marketing, and use of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, with a particular focus on high-risk applications. This set of guidelines and requirements is designed to ensure compliance with Union values and protect fundamental rights while fostering innovation among its members and associated projects.

The Regulation establishes detailed rules regarding the classification and operational procedures specifically tailored to high-risk AI systems, clearly delineating the responsibilities of various stakeholders, including deployers, notified bodies, subcontractors, and subsidiaries. This clarity is essential for ensuring adherence to legal standards. Critical compliance measures emphasized by the Regulation include data privacy protections, careful management of confidential information, and lawful processing of biometric data, enhancing safeguards in both civilian and military contexts.

Furthermore, the Regulation promotes non-discriminatory practices to ensure objectivity in sensitive sectors, such as law enforcement and migration. It provides explicit guidelines governing the processing of biometric data by competent authorities, with a priority on health, safety, and protection of individual rights. The aim is to improve the functionality of the internal market while fostering a human-centric approach to AI technology.

To hold AI providers accountable, the Regulation mandates transparency for high-risk AI systems prior to their market entry. Operators are required to detect and disclose outputs that have been artificially generated or manipulated. Additionally, the Regulation establishes classification criteria for general-purpose AI models that may pose systemic risks based on their capabilities and the computational resources utilized during training.

In summary, the Regulation serves as a vital legal framework governing the responsibilities of AI model providers, addressing ethical considerations in AI deployment, including the use of emotion recognition systems related to biometric data. It reinforces the importance of legal standards, obligations, and the protection of individual rights in advancing AI technologies, outlining necessary actions and compliance measures for providers of general-purpose AI models, as well as the enforcement process and expert consultation for Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation encompasses the legal requirements for AI model providers, focusing on risk identification and cybersecurity protections.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation aims to enhance the internal market for AI by promoting human-centric and trustworthy systems while ensuring health and safety protections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714d9f621f6eee9273625419653b083c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a57bbcc3ccf00f26352f12c36036aedf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e7ae4f78080133a8770768bccbc462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70337c5367702b9a8ef4dd8a241aa46d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b28a4b325cc05a6cc4897f58ccdf00f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-239d42cf353b4be7fdeade1f3fced85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18d33fd192f06f727ac6bb21becbaa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac04e8bc9dd9ff3998ce3c08f3800f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e215b390ecf16d1806ebe2ba8ac2c33d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5fb48082255c480535475ddb098366a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6579442a2f027e643cf907006333003a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af20