    <node id="Military">
      <data key="d0">Military</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Military refers to the organized armed forces of a country, responsible for defending the state and its interests, often involving defense and national security operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Defense">
      <data key="d0">Defense</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Defense is a governmental responsibility that involves protecting the state against external threats and ensuring military preparedness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement encompasses a network of government agencies and personnel dedicated to maintaining public order, enforcing laws, and preventing and investigating crime. As an organized body, it is responsible not only for crime prevention and victim identification but also for the regulation of technologies utilized in its operations, particularly biometric identification systems. These systems can facilitate real-time identification in public spaces, assisting law enforcement agencies in carrying out their functions effectively.

The involvement of law enforcement in the application of such technologies is governed by specific regulations and verification processes established by national or union law. This regulatory framework emphasizes the high-risk nature of deploying artificial intelligence (AI) systems within the sector, ensuring that their implementation aligns with legal standards aimed at safeguarding public safety and protecting individual rights.

Overall, Law Enforcement represents a critical system committed to the prevention, detection, and investigation of criminal activities while upholding the rule of law and ensuring the safety of the public. It encompasses government agencies and officials who utilize various tools, including advanced technologies for surveillance and identification, as part of their mandate to enforce laws and maintain social order.&lt;SEP&gt;Law Enforcement refers to the bodies responsible for maintaining order and enforcing the law, which may have special needs regarding the use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2035e81a92cf42f945220e637e40591a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b92a727425c41637e16da3cb9ac9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83317eda1161cf5d13ef9aa07297c98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab148daacc5693b15ec462635a5502a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-737358b61293029e1a6d7326160654fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_94.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936285</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of AI Systems are businesses or organizations that create and supply artificial intelligence technologies. They operate under the regulations set by the Union and are responsible for adhering to ethical standards. These entities can be individuals or organizations that develop AI technologies and participate in regulatory sandboxes, which allow them to demonstrate compliance with regulatory requirements. Providers of AI Systems are involved in both military and civilian applications of artificial intelligence solutions. Furthermore, they create and submit applications to participate in AI regulatory sandboxes, where they can test their technologies. Ultimately, these providers bear the responsibility for the creation, deployment, and ethical implementation of AI technologies, all while being subjected to regulatory obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems are companies or entities that integrate various components, tools, and services into AI systems for various applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI systems are responsible for ensuring that their systems designed to interact directly with people inform users when they are interacting with AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI systems are entities or businesses responsible for the creation and deployment of AI technologies, aiming to meet regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714d9f621f6eee9273625419653b083c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_165.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_136.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936187</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Level">
      <data key="d0">National Level</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National level refers to the jurisdiction of national authorities regarding registration and oversight of high-risk AI systems in their respective countries.&lt;SEP&gt;The national level refers to the specific governmental and regulatory frameworks applied within individual countries that align with Union regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935023</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intellectual Property Rights">
      <data key="d0">Intellectual Property Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intellectual Property Rights are legal rights that grant creators control over the use of their creations, including patents and trade secrets.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual Property Rights are legal rights that protect creations of the mind, such as inventions, designs, and artistic works, ensuring their creators can control their use.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual Property Rights are legal rights that grant creators protection over their inventions, designs, and brands related to AI innovations.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights encompass legal rights that grant creators protection over their inventions, designs, and artistic works, ensuring that their innovations are not improperly used by others.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4d7c8b1c65cb7b9f5021681b13c271</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidential Business Information">
      <data key="d0">Confidential Business Information</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidential Business Information encompasses sensitive data that companies wish to keep secret to maintain competitive advantage, including trade secrets and source codes.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential Business Information includes proprietary data that companies wish to keep private to maintain competitiveness and secure their trade secrets.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential Business Information refers to proprietary and sensitive information necessary for maintaining competitive advantages and legal compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential business information consists of sensitive data that companies wish to keep secret to maintain competitive advantage, including trade secrets and proprietary knowledge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4d7c8b1c65cb7b9f5021681b13c271</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trade Secrets">
      <data key="d0">Trade Secrets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade Secrets are forms of confidential business information that organizations seek to protect from disclosure, particularly in the context of AI training data and development. They include practices, designs, formulas, processes, and any information that grants a business a competitive edge over its competitors who do not know or use this information. Trade Secrets are specifically protected under various national and union laws, as well as confidentiality obligations. This protection ensures that the economic advantage provided by such confidential information is maintained, as it remains private and not publicly known.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fce1cda52753ec9e5183762f5b2c81b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4d08c48923bc3e8bff8968fd67a799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4d7c8b1c65cb7b9f5021681b13c271</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality involves the obligation of notified bodies to protect sensitive information obtained during conformity assessment activities from unauthorized disclosure.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality refers to the ethical principle of keeping sensitive information private and secure against unauthorized access or disclosure.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality pertains to the safeguarding of sensitive information obtained during compliance monitoring and regulatory processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality is a principle that requires keeping certain information secure and private, particularly sensitive data obtained during conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a310ed4ba9b96c860daae9a944f07fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Law">
      <data key="d0">National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Law encompasses the legal codes and regulations established within a country to protect the rights of individuals and corporations.&lt;SEP&gt;National Law encompasses the legal frameworks and regulations established by individual countries, governing a wide range of areas, including individual rights related to public spaces, security, and the application of biometric identification technologies for law enforcement. It comprises all laws enacted by a country's legislative body, which must be aligned with overarching Union regulations to ensure effective governance and compliance with broader legal standards set by the Union. 

Variations in National Law exist from one Member State to another, as each country's legal framework reflects its internal affairs while addressing specific rights and obligations. This legal structure not only regulates business information confidentiality and trade secrets but also issues related to conformity assessments and liability. Furthermore, National Law plays a crucial role in the operation and regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly in relation to Union law.

In addition, National Law refers to domestic legislation enacted by individual countries aimed at protecting various rights, including intellectual property rights and confidential business information. It governs processes related to the use of AI systems, as well as migration and border control regulations, all while ensuring compatibility with European Union regulations. Ultimately, National Law serves as the essential legal structure that oversees significant aspects of life within a country, balancing national interests with broader legal requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;National law represents individual country regulations concerning the implementation and oversight of AI systems, including potential exemptions for certain cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2035e81a92cf42f945220e637e40591a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4d7c8b1c65cb7b9f5021681b13c271&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c664ec81872dda212b64d449aa7a2014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e</data>
