    <node id="Integrity of Criminal Proceedings">
      <data key="d0">Integrity of Criminal Proceedings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Integrity of Criminal Proceedings ensures that legal processes are conducted fairly, upholding the principles of justice and due process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_167.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Integrity of Classified Information">
      <data key="d0">Integrity of Classified Information</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Integrity of Classified Information involves protecting sensitive government or military information from unauthorized access and dissemination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_167.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI HLEG">
      <data key="d0">AI HLEG</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI HLEG is an independent expert group appointed by the European Commission to provide guidelines for trustworthy AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934136</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Commission">
      <data key="d0">European Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Commission is a crucial institution within the European Union, serving as its executive body. It plays a significant role in proposing legislation, enforcing laws, and managing the day-to-day operations of the EU. Among its many responsibilities, the European Commission oversees the development and implementation of policies related to artificial intelligence (AI), ensuring that AI systems adhere to EU treaties and regulations.

In its capacity as a regulator of AI, the European Commission has the authority to access reports generated from AI regulatory sandboxes, actively participate in regulatory enforcement, and appoint experts responsible for evaluating AI models. The Commission also adopts implementing acts that establish relevant regulations and sets post-market monitoring requirements to guarantee the compliance and safety of AI technologies.

Additionally, the European Commission is tasked with developing guidelines to ensure that AI systems meet established standards, emphasizing its pivotal role in shaping and regulating the AI landscape in Europe. This comprehensive oversight showcases the Commission's integral part in both the governance of the EU and the management of advanced technologies, particularly AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a48f68b8943ab2f8e6bdbb9ccf3e17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f</data>
