    <node id="AI Models">
      <data key="d0">AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Models refer to computational frameworks used for artificial intelligence applications, which must comply with specific regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Models refer to general-purpose artificial intelligence systems that undergo pre-training and training using various datasets and data collections.&lt;SEP&gt;AI models refer to the algorithms and systems used to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, subject to regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Models refer to general-purpose artificial intelligence systems that present systemic risks and require specific regulatory obligations for their providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5c4d08c48923bc3e8bff8968fd67a799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Office">
      <data key="d0">AI Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Office is a dedicated regulatory body under The Commission of the European Union, established to develop expertise and capabilities in the field of artificial intelligence (AI). Its primary mission involves overseeing the implementation and governance of AI systems within the Union, ensuring compliance with established codes of practice and regulations while representing the interests of various stakeholders in the AI landscape.

As a crucial entity within The Commission, the AI Office is tasked with multiple responsibilities, including market surveillance, particularly concerning high-risk AI systems and the assessment of general-purpose AI models. This encompasses monitoring compliance with legal standards, evaluating systemic risks associated with AI technologies, and conducting evaluations to address any possible infringements by providers of AI models.

The AI Office develops and recommends voluntary model terms for contracts related to AI systems, creating templates and guidelines for summarizing AI model training content. It also maintains a comprehensive list of planned and existing AI regulatory sandboxes and coordinates support for investigations related to high-risk AI systems as defined under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.

Furthermore, the office develops methodologies for risk evaluation associated with AI systems and supervises their integration into specific regulatory frameworks. It actively engages with diverse stakeholders, including the scientific community and industry players, to assess systemic risks, establish methodologies, and set thresholds for categorizing AI models, thereby enhancing compliance with regulatory standards. 

In addition to these responsibilities, the AI Office provides secretariat support for the Board, organizing meetings, preparing agendas, and coordinating alerts. It assists the scientific panel in its tasks and promotes the development and revision of codes of practice for general-purpose AI models. The office strives to incorporate international approaches and diverse perspectives into its regulatory framework while assessing the adequacy of codes of practice and harmonized standards related to the compliance obligations of AI providers.

Overall, the AI Office serves as a critical authority focused on the oversight, compliance, and risk assessment of AI technologies, ensuring that AI model providers adhere not only to Union copyright law but also to a broader set of regulatory obligations. Through its governance and collaborative efforts, the AI Office effectively addresses the complexities and challenges posed by the rapid advancement of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is responsible for monitoring the implementation of regulations related to general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is responsible for monitoring activities related to general-purpose AI models and addressing potential risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcc9707fb1611da88a5526a5558a165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4d08c48923bc3e8bff8968fd67a799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6579442a2f027e643cf907006333003a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f4621c3d73dca675e991da5d0c9317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0a