    </node>
    <node id="Lifecycle of AI System">
      <data key="d0">Lifecycle of AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The lifecycle of an AI system includes all stages from development to deployment and monitoring, emphasizing the need for ongoing risk management throughout these stages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ca7c773df7242c37f506b8ad3db475b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Risk Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk assessment involves estimating and evaluating known and foreseeable risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk assessment involves evaluating the severity and impact of incidents related to AI systems to inform corrective actions and regulatory responses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ca7c773df7242c37f506b8ad3db475b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mitigation Measures">
      <data key="d0">Mitigation Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Mitigation measures are specific strategies and actions implemented to reduce, control, or eliminate identified risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation measures are strategies designed to reduce or eliminate risks associated with the deployment of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ca7c773df7242c37f506b8ad3db475b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_116.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935542</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 60">
      <data key="d0">Article 60</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 60 discusses guidelines surrounding the accessibility and visibility of the information contained in the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 outlines requirements for obtaining informed consent from subjects in testing scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 outlines testing procedures for high-risk AI systems in real-world conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 pertains to specific regulations and guidelines for the testing and compliance of high-risk AI systems in real-world conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 provides the compliance conditions that AI systems must meet when tested in real-world scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_61.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management Measures">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk Management Measures refer to the procedures and strategies implemented to eliminate or mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems during their lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk management measures refer to the strategies and methodologies used to identify, assess, and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems during their lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Residual Risk">
      <data key="d0">Residual Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Residual Risk signifies the risk remaining after risk management efforts have been applied to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hazard">
      <data key="d0">Hazard</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Hazard is any source of potential damage, harm, or adverse effect on people, property, or the environment in the context of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployer">
      <data key="d0">Deployer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A deployer is defined as any natural or legal person, including public authorities and agencies, who use an AI system under its authority.&lt;SEP&gt;The Deployer is defined as an individual or organization tasked with the deployment and operational management of high-risk AI systems. This entity is responsible for installing or configuring these systems, ensuring they are used effectively and responsibly within the confines of established guidelines and safety measures set forth by the Provider. The Deployer operates under the authority of the Provider, managing the implementation and oversight of the AI systems while ensuring compliance with legal obligations, including transparency and the rights of affected individuals.

In addition to overseeing the operation of these high-risk AI systems, the Deployer has a duty to adhere to specific oversight protocols and is obligated to report any serious incidents associated with the deployed systems to relevant authorities. This entity may include public law bodies or private entities providing public services and is responsible for conducting assessments in accordance with regulatory requirements. Furthermore, the Deployer must ensure that the AI systems are registered and monitored as specified by applicable regulations. In summary, the Deployer plays a critical role in the ethical and responsible deployment of high-risk AI technologies, emphasizing compliance, accountability, and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployer indicates any body that implements or uses the AI system in real-world scenarios, participating in the testing process.&lt;SEP&gt;The deployer is the individual or organization using the AI system and is responsible for adhering to the guidelines and instructions provided by the provider.&lt;SEP&gt;The deployer refers to any party that implements or uses the high-risk AI system, which must adhere to guidelines provided by the provider.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b28a4b325cc05a6cc4897f58ccdf00f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936040</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Testing Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing Procedures refer to the methods and processes used to ensure high-risk AI systems meet defined metrics and performance standards before going to market.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing procedures are methods employed to evaluate high-risk AI systems to ensure they meet defined performance metrics and safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Training Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training Requirements pertain to the necessary educational and skill-based training that must be provided to deployers of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Groups">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulnerable groups encompass a range of individuals who are more susceptible to the negative impacts of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This includes individuals living in extreme poverty, racial and ethnic minorities, people with disabilities, and minors under the age of 18. These populations are identified as being at greater risk of exploitation and harmful consequences from manipulative or high-risk AI systems. 

The vulnerabilities experienced by these groups may stem from systemic discrimination and inherent biases embedded within AI technologies. As such, regulatory evaluations give particular attention to these populations, recognizing their heightened risk of adverse effects from AI decisions. Furthermore, it is essential to provide these groups with additional protections during AI testing to mitigate potential risks and ensure their safety. Overall, the term "vulnerable groups" refers to specific demographics that require careful consideration and protective measures in the context of AI development and implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups refer to individuals who may be at greater risk due to age or disability and require special consideration in interactions with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936285</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing in Real-World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Testing in Real-World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing in real-world conditions involves evaluating high-risk AI systems in environments that simulate their intended use to ensure they perform reliably.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2019/1020">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2019/1020</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 is a European legislative framework that governs market surveillance practices and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 is a legislative framework in the European Union that addresses various aspects of general-purpose AI models and their providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 is a significant piece of legislation established by the European Union that addresses market surveillance and compliance for products within the EU, with a particular emphasis on high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This regulation is designed to ensure the safety of goods entering the European market, fundamentally focusing on protecting health, safety, and individual rights.

The regulation provides a comprehensive legal framework that outlines the authority and procedures necessary for monitoring AI systems and other products, ensuring they adhere to established safety and performance standards. It enhances existing regulations by promoting responsible introduction and use of AI technologies, thereby improving product safety within the EU.

Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 delineates the responsibilities of market surveillance authorities and establishes clear guidelines for compliance among economic operators. It also allows for the submission of complaints regarding infringements of its rules and specifies the actions to be taken to enforce compliance across Member States.

Overall, Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 serves as a critical legal structure for the enforcement of compliance laws governing AI systems, contributing to enhanced safety and efficiency of products in the market while protecting consumers and upholding individual rights throughout the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 is a legal framework that outlines procedures for ensuring the compliance of products within the EU, particularly regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 outlines the requirements and powers related to market surveillance of AI systems, including oversight and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ff05678672211287e9053ebcd9c1c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40de45b5b0c24b78b7ef2ca4e835c29c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8affbc363cca00e716c4494cb81a558a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_94.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_161.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_156.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_149.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance Authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing compliance with market regulations, including those related to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority refers to regulatory bodies operating within Member States of the European Union, tasked with monitoring and enforcing compliance with regulations, particularly concerning high-risk AI systems. Acting as contact points, these authorities play a crucial role in overseeing the deployment of advanced technologies and ensuring adherence to market regulations and EU harmonization legislation.

Among its primary responsibilities, the Market Surveillance Authority is charged with enforcing product safety regulations and legal standards, with a strong focus on high-risk AI systems. This includes handling complaints related to regulatory infringements and conducting extensive market surveillance activities to evaluate compliance with regulatory requirements. The Authority supervises the authorization of high-risk products and mandates that market participants adhere to stringent safety standards, especially in sensitive areas such as law enforcement.

Furthermore, the Market Surveillance Authority is dedicated to promoting accountability and safety within the market. It oversees the implementation of regulations related to high-risk AI systems and ensures compliance with health, safety, and environmental protection standards across the European Union. By monitoring and regulating critical technologies, the Authority helps mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI applications, safeguarding public health and safety.

In summary, the Market Surveillance Authority is a vital institution responsible for evaluating AI systems, enforcing conformity and compliance with safety and performance standards, and overseeing the regulation of high-risk AI systems in EU Member States. Its comprehensive market surveillance activities ensure that products are tested in real-world conditions and that the principles of public interest and safety are upheld.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Authorities are regulatory bodies that oversee the compliance of AI systems and ensure adherence to established guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c</data>
