      <data key="d5">1783936287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaint">
      <data key="d0">Complaint</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Complaint is a formal notice lodged by downstream providers alleging an infringement of the Regulation by the providers of general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;A complaint is a formal expression of dissatisfaction, regarding a perceived infringement of provisions under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 that can be submitted to market surveillance authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18d33fd192f06f727ac6bb21becbaa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936303</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Activities">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance Activities refer to the processes undertaken by authorities to ensure compliance with financial regulations and monitor market integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance activities are efforts undertaken to monitor financial markets to ensure compliance with regulations and maintain fair trading practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance activities involve monitoring and ensuring compliance with regulations to safeguard market integrity and public interest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An infringement is a violation of established regulations, which may lead to administrative fines and enforcement actions by relevant authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;An infringement refers to a violation of laws or regulations, which may lead to administrative fines and enforcement actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Infringement refers to the violation or breach of the provisions set forth in the regulation, which may lead to complaints being filed.&lt;SEP&gt;Infringement refers to violations of data protection regulations that can lead to penalties imposed by the European Data Protection Supervisor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance Authorities are designated bodies established by Member States to ensure compliance with regulatory standards across various sectors, including artificial intelligence (AI), financial services, and other markets. Their primary role involves monitoring and enforcing adherence to EU regulations and laws, which is essential for maintaining the safety and efficacy of products in the market. These authorities play a pivotal role in safeguarding consumer interests through their surveillance activities and investigations concerning regulatory compliance.

Specifically, Market Surveillance Authorities focus on overseeing high-risk AI systems as mandated by EU directives, ensuring these systems conform to established EU guidelines. They are tasked with enforcing safety measures, conducting thorough inspections, and maintaining oversight in the marketplace. This includes monitoring products in real-world testing conditions to ensure compliance with regulatory standards, thereby reinforcing the integrity of the market environment.

In addition to compliance monitoring, Market Surveillance Authorities have the authority to impose administrative fines for violations, underlining the significance of adherence to market regulations. They are also involved in discussions within various sub-groups of regulatory bodies, contributing to the collaborative efforts in shaping and upholding market regulations.

Overall, Market Surveillance Authorities are crucial entities responsible for ensuring that products and services meet regulatory standards while protecting consumers and upholding the principles outlined in the Union's harmonization legislation, specifically as specified in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Their comprehensive efforts are vital for the effective regulation and monitoring of diverse market activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Authorities are tasked with overseeing the market for compliance with applicable regulations, particularly concerning AI systems and products.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are responsible for monitoring compliance and safeguarding information relevant to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are regulatory bodies tasked with ensuring compliance and safe testing of AI systems in real-world conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Authorities oversee compliance with regulations and may request information from notified bodies regarding conformity assessment activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_156.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936324</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 16">
      <data key="d0">Article 16</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 16 outlines legal obligations for providers of high-risk AI systems, specifying compliance requirements related to product safety and manufacturer responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 specifies the obligations of providers for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 specifies the obligations and responsibilities of providers and importers of high-risk AI systems under EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934471</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 85">
      <data key="d0">Recital 85</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 85 provides context for the Regulation related to high-risk AI systems and their providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 84">
      <data key="d0">Recital 84</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 84 provides additional context important for understanding the Regulation regarding high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 86">
      <data key="d0">Recital 86</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 86 addresses compliance obligations for initial providers of high-risk AI systems regarding information and technical access needed for regulation adherence.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 86 delineates the conditions under which the initial provider of a high-risk AI system is no longer considered a provider.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 87">
      <data key="d0">Recital 87</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 87 outlines specific conditions when the product manufacturer is deemed the provider of the high-risk AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 87 outlines the obligations of product manufacturers concerning high-risk AI systems that are safety components included with their products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider">
      <data key="d0">Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Provider refers to individuals or entities offering AI systems to the market and may challenge decisions made by regulatory authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Provider refers to any specific natural or legal person who assumes responsibility for the placement and deployment of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems in the market. This entity is crucial in organizing and conducting testing of AI systems in real-world conditions to ensure compliance with applicable regulations. Providers may include individuals or organizations that are responsible for the development, supply, and oversight of AI technologies, particularly those applications deemed as high-risk.

Providers have several core responsibilities, which include ensuring compliance with established regulatory standards, maintaining thorough documentation to meet legal requirements, and demonstrating accountability for the intended uses of their AI systems. A significant part of their duties involves assessing the risks associated with AI technologies prior to marketing or deployment, as well as implementing measures to mitigate potential risks. 

Furthermore, Providers must establish and uphold a sound quality management system, particularly when dealing with high-risk AI systems. They engage in regulatory sandboxes to rigorously test their AI solutions to ensure legal adherence. Their roles span various functions, such as distributors, importers, and deployers of these AI systems, all of which are carried out under strict regulatory scrutiny.

In addition to their operational responsibilities, Providers are also tasked with reporting incidents related to their AI systems and conducting investigations as mandated. Legal representation is often necessary to navigate the complex landscape of AI-related laws and regulations. When an AI system is classified as a general-purpose model with potential systemic risks, Providers must appropriately respond to requests concerning its designation and ensure the accuracy and reliability of the information provided by their systems.

Overall, Providers play a pivotal role in making high-risk AI systems available in the market while adhering to stringent regulatory obligations and facing the repercussions of non-compliance, including potential fines. Their accountability within the operational ecosystem of AI reinforces the importance of their roles in promoting safe and responsible AI development and deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is an entity or individual responsible for the deployment and management of AI systems within regulated environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19283d37b8085eb0b86aff77d85558de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0c14a128bfd78c4c5056f7102cc152&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5406d942407c55f04629004d833f8196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_128.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A high-risk AI system is a classification of AI technology that poses significant risks and requires designated responsibilities for its deployment and service.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Risk AI Systems are a classification of artificial intelligence technologies recognized for their potential to pose significant risks to health, safety, and fundamental rights. They are characterized by their advanced capabilities, which can lead to substantial harm if not properly regulated. As such, these systems are subject to strict regulatory oversight and compliance with established standards prior to being marketed and used.

Providers, distributors, and importers of High-Risk AI Systems are legally required to ensure adherence to specific regulatory requirements, which include implementing necessary modifications to meet compliance standards. The classification of these systems is fundamentally informed by their potential impact on public safety, individual rights, and the broader societal implications of their deployment.

To guarantee safe and effective operation, High-Risk AI Systems necessitate rigorous monitoring and compliance checks. This extends to strict adherence to data governance and management practices designed to minimize bias and discrimination in their operation. Consequently, a thorough regulatory approval process is essential before these systems can be made available for public use, as it is crucial for mitigating risks and protecting users and the broader market.

Overall, High-Risk AI Systems are subject to stricter legal requirements due to the significant risks they present to health, safety, and fundamental rights, making regulatory compliance a key component of their development and deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Risk AI Systems are those AI products deemed to pose significant risks to health, safety, and fundamental rights, and thus require stricter regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Risk AI Systems refer to specific AI systems categorized under stringent regulations to ensure safety, health, and fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are automated systems that may pose significant risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights and require compliance checks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19283d37b8085eb0b86aff77d85558de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
