      <data key="d5">1783936210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market">
      <data key="d0">Market</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Market refers to the commercial environment where high-risk AI systems are sold and distributed. It serves as a commercial platform that makes AI systems available for distribution, whether for a fee or free of charge. This market encompasses the space where AI systems are sold and used, involving various stakeholders such as providers and distributors. The term "market" also describes the conditions affecting both providers and users, highlighting the economic landscape where General-Purpose AI Models are accessible for various applications, downloads, and services. Overall, the Market functions as a platform or environment where products and services, including AI systems, are offered for sale or trade, thereby facilitating interaction among various participants in the AI ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market refers to the economic environment in which goods and services, such as high-risk AI systems, are offered for sale or service.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market refers to the environment where AI models are offered to consumers and businesses, requiring compliance with safety and security regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759ef1bca08a56dec0192e47771d9820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_123.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance assessment involves evaluating AI systems to ensure they meet established regulations and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance assessment refers to the process through which AI systems are evaluated to meet regulatory standards for safety and ethical considerations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c168b1207668ad4ba646371f91bfce09</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_124.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934911</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Harmonisation Legislation">
      <data key="d0">Union Harmonisation Legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Harmonisation Legislation is a comprehensive set of regulations and legal frameworks established by the European Union, aimed at ensuring consistency and compliance across various sectors, including artificial intelligence (AI) and product safety. This legislation seeks to create uniform product standards throughout EU member states, thereby facilitating the free movement of goods within the internal market while safeguarding consumer safety and ensuring compliance with essential safety and quality standards.

The Union Harmonisation Legislation includes various laws and directives that standardize regulatory practices related to product conformity assessments. This encompasses specific provisions for sectors such as medical devices and high-risk AI systems, influencing the obligations of providers within these domains. Through its framework, the legislation guarantees that products meet safety and performance standards before being marketed within the EU, significantly impacting the testing and compliance processes for high-risk AI systems.

Overall, the Union Harmonisation Legislation plays a critical role in fostering trade among EU countries by promoting regulatory uniformity, ensuring that products not only comply with EU laws but also adhere to established safety and health standards across all member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to the body of laws aimed at ensuring consistent standards and regulations across the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation encompasses a set of rules established by the European Union to ensure the safety and efficacy of products in the market, influencing how AI systems are classified.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to the legal frameworks established by the European Union to standardize regulations across member states, particularly regarding product safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70555b8168fcbd401cc11093ec15091a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18cf1aa30864348514b20fe64038fba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efd21db4fc63a879493cbb376ae904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ab1f3b6cbb052c58ff3b9fc75a6d7a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_128.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_87.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_147.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935947</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Product Manufacturer">
      <data key="d0">Product Manufacturer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The product manufacturer is identified as the entity responsible for placing a high-risk AI system in the market, under specific regulatory obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;The product manufacturer is responsible for ensuring that products comply with relevant legislation and safety requirements, including regulations governing embedded AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems are a classification of artificial intelligence technologies that are recognized for their significant implications for safety, privacy, and fundamental rights. These systems typically arise in contexts that involve considerable risks, such as the workplace and law enforcement. Given their potential impact on health and safety, high-risk AI systems are subject to strict regulatory oversight.

According to the regulatory framework established by the European Union, high-risk AI systems must be registered and must adhere to comprehensive compliance requirements that ensure their safety and conformity prior to market entry. This involves the implementation of robust quality management systems aimed at mitigating risks associated with their operation. The specific technologies classified as high-risk are identified in Annex III of the relevant legislation, which mandates thorough regulatory scrutiny and conformity assessment procedures to protect individual rights and public welfare across multiple Member States.

Furthermore, these systems are defined by the EU regulations as needing extensive testing to confirm their compliance with legal and ethical standards, particularly in sensitive fields such as law enforcement and asylum. Consequently, high-risk AI systems demand rigorous certification, monitoring, and assessment before they can be deployed, reflecting their potential impact on health, safety, and fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to AI technologies that are classified under strict regulatory standards due to their potential impact on safety and security.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are systems classified under regulations that pose significant risks and require compliance evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to artificial intelligence technologies that present significant risks and require careful contractual terms regarding their use and integration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad25bfaa86145b8556e5d82696b8bab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-595952fa3e7e47cb312adaaad303b73c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60a12c037b4dee54159c11f348ff3f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_122.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_146.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936290</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union harmonisation legislation">
      <data key="d0">Union harmonisation legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union harmonisation legislation encompasses laws and directives aimed at ensuring the safety and compliance of products within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation encompasses rules and standards established to ensure uniformity in compliance practices across the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to laws that ensure products meet common standards across the European Union, applicable to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to legislative frameworks in the European Union aimed at ensuring product compliance and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation encompasses various laws in the EU intended to align product safety standards and regulations across member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c168b1207668ad4ba646371f91bfce09</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_124.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935777</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 88">
      <data key="d0">Recital 88</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 88 discusses the necessity of specifying information and capabilities for third parties supplying components integrated into high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 89">
      <data key="d0">Recital 89</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 89 elaborates on the conditions under which third-party tools and services for high-risk AI systems must be made accessible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 90">
      <data key="d0">Recital 90</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 90 highlights the importance of observing and protecting intellectual property rights and trade secrets associated with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="initial provider">
      <data key="d0">initial provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The initial provider is responsible for closely cooperating with new providers and ensuring the availability of information required for the fulfillment of obligations related to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="new providers">
      <data key="d0">new providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">New providers are entities that collaborate with the initial provider to comply with regulations surrounding high-risk AI systems and may require assistance and access to necessary information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="third party">
      <data key="d0">third party</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Third parties supply AI systems, tools, services, components, or processes utilized within high-risk AI systems and must comply with specific agreements with the high-risk AI system provider.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="conformity assessment">
      <data key="d0">conformity assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity assessment is the process used to determine whether a high-risk AI system meets regulatory requirements and is safe for use.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment refers to the evaluation process that determines whether high-risk AI systems meet specific regulatory safety standards as outlined in the legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union law">
      <data key="d0">Union law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law comprises the comprehensive legal norms and regulations that govern the member states of the European Union (EU). It establishes the rights and responsibilities of these states, ensuring compliance with various frameworks and protections across multiple domains. This includes regulations pertinent to areas such as artificial intelligence (AI), intellectual property rights, and trade secrets, as well as specific directives related to biometric identification systems and data protection.

Essentially, Union law is built upon the treaties, regulations, directives, and decisions enacted by the EU, forming a cohesive legal framework that member states must adhere to. This legal structure not only influences the governance of AI systems but also incorporates critical aspects like CE marking—a certification marking that indicates conformity with health, safety, and environmental protection standards in products sold within the European Economic Area. Overall, Union law serves as the backbone of legal order within the EU, affecting a wide array of civil rights and protections.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to the body of laws that govern the European Union, including regulations on copyright and related rights applicable to AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_172.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Third parties are entities that provide tools, services, components, or processes to AI system providers, and may be subject to regulatory terms.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties refer to external entities that provide certified compliance services, verifying data governance and integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties refer to organizations or entities that provide tools, services, processes, or AI components to the public.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties are external entities that supply tools, services, components, or processes needed for the integration or operation of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936290</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voluntary Model Terms">
      <data key="d0">Voluntary Model Terms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Voluntary Model Terms are recommendations made by the AI Office for contracts between providers of high-risk AI systems and third-party suppliers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tools and Services">
      <data key="d0">Tools and Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Tools and Services encompass the resources provided by third parties to assist in the development and use of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Tools and services encapsulate various applications and functions related to artificial intelligence that are provided to users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Components and Processes">
      <data key="d0">Components and Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Components and Processes refer to the integral parts and operations involved in AI systems that third parties may supply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="intellectual property rights">
      <data key="d0">intellectual property rights</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law safeguards intellectual property rights integral to the development and deployment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorised Representative">
      <data key="d0">Authorised Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An authorised representative is a person in the Union who carries out obligations on behalf of a provider of an AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Authorised Representative acts on behalf of the provider, especially in regulatory compliance matters concerning AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Authorised Representative is a designated individual or organization appointed by a provider to act on its behalf within the Union, ensuring compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Authorised Representative is a designated individual or entity representing non-EU AI system providers to ensure compliance with Union regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fc29985a43f3bd521b3a1c9eb9ba756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_82.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importer">
      <data key="d0">Importer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An Importer is an individual or entity in the Union that brings AI systems from third countries into the market under their name.&lt;SEP&gt;An importer is a person or entity in the Union that places an AI system on the market under a foreign trademark.&lt;SEP&gt;The importer is the organization or individual that brings the high-risk AI system into the market, ensuring it meets local compliance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;An importer is an entity that brings goods from another country for sale, and it is subject to the same obligations regarding high-risk AI systems as distributors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934633</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributor">
      <data key="d0">Distributor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Distributor is an entity or individual involved in the supply chain that plays a crucial role in making high-risk AI systems accessible in the Union market. This entity is responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations related to these AI systems and must address any issues reported by deployers. In addition to facilitating market access, a Distributor may sell products directly to consumers or to retailers and is considered a high-risk AI system provider if it affixes its name to the system. These responsibilities include not only distribution but also the obligation to implement corrective actions as necessary to align with regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934873</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operator">
      <data key="d0">Operator</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An Operator refers to any individual or entity responsible for managing or deploying AI systems, encompassing various roles in the supply chain.&lt;SEP&gt;An operator is anyone involved in the supply chain of an AI system, including providers, importers, distributors, and others.&lt;SEP&gt;Operator refers to entities or individuals who manage or oversee the functioning of AI systems, particularly in the context of compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935856</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI system">
      <data key="d0">AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI system encompasses various technologies and frameworks that utilize artificial intelligence, subject to compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems refer to technological systems that leverage artificial intelligence for a range of applications, adhering to specific regulations. These systems are designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy and exhibit adaptiveness, allowing them to generate predictions, recommendations, or decisions based on input data. AI systems perform tasks typically requiring human intelligence, demonstrating the ability to learn and adapt to new information over time. Additionally, AI technologies can generate or manipulate content, including images, audio, or video, which may closely resemble real entities or events. Due to their potential impact, AI systems are subject to regulatory frameworks, particularly concerning their purpose and the implications of non-compliance with established regulations under Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI system refers to technology that utilizes artificial intelligence to generate content and assist in various applications, addressing obligations for transparency and accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI system refers to the technological framework used for biometric identification and law enforcement purposes, including data processing and identification.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI system refers to a set of technologies and algorithms designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, with considerations for data privacy and protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ba08954f9ed754c2566e3c59b63ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d18c3755735a13a436e766a5ca73fc4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935923</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk">
      <data key="d0">Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk is defined as the combination of the probability of harm occurring and the severity of that harm, important for evaluating AI system impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The General-Purpose AI Model is an advanced artificial intelligence system designed to perform a diverse array of tasks across multiple domains. Its flexibility and adaptability make it suitable for integration into various AI applications. This model exemplifies the ongoing evolution of AI technology, demonstrating sophisticated capabilities that enhance its functionality in different sectors, including professional fields such as law.

While the General-Purpose AI Model showcases significant advancements in AI applications, it also raises concerns regarding systemic risks. Regulatory bodies, including governing authorities such as the AI Office, have established frameworks to assess and manage these risks effectively. Compliance with these regulatory standards is crucial to ensure the safe and responsible deployment of General-Purpose AI Models in various settings.

Overall, the General-Purpose AI Model underscores the importance of balancing the growing capabilities of artificial intelligence with the need for careful management and oversight to mitigate potential risks associated with its use. Its versatility positions it as a key player in the broader landscape of AI technologies, highlighting the importance of responsible development and regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5406d942407c55f04629004d833f8196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8033b978339bfb2f89fde823ffa3f524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8affbc363cca00e716c4494cb81a558a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_94.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935993</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Component">
      <data key="d0">Safety Component</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Safety Component is an integral part of an AI system designed to ensure safety and prevent health or property hazards.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety Component is an element of an AI system that ensures safety and compliance, crucial for preventing harm to people or property.&lt;SEP&gt;A safety component is a part of a product designed to ensure safety and reliability, which may include high-risk AI systems under regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_87.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Instructions for Use">
      <data key="d0">Instructions for Use</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Instructions for Use are the guidelines provided by the provider to inform users about the AI system's intended application and proper utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for Use consist of information provided by the Provider detailing the intended purpose and correct usage of an AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for use are accompanying documents that outline how to safely and effectively operate high-risk AI systems, including their functionalities and limitations.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for use are essential documents that provide guidance on the proper deployment and limitations of AI systems, ensuring comprehensibility for target deployers.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for use are the guidelines provided along with high-risk AI systems, detailing how to operate them safely and effectively in compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935672</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recall of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Recall of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recall of an AI System describes the process of retrieving an AI product that has been made available in the market, typically due to safety concerns or non-compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Withdrawal of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Withdrawal of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Withdrawal of an AI System is a measure to remove an AI product from the market due to safety, regulatory, or compliance issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reasonably Foreseeable Misuse">
      <data key="d0">Reasonably Foreseeable Misuse</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Reasonably Foreseeable Misuse encompasses the potential misuse of an AI system that is not intended but can occur due to human behavior or interaction with other systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Reasonably Foreseeable Misuse refers to potential improper uses of an AI system that may arise from expected human behavior or interaction with the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notifying Authority">
      <data key="d0">Notifying Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Notifying Authority is an organization or governmental body designated within each Member State, tasked with a critical role in the regulatory framework for high-risk AI systems. Its primary responsibilities include designating notified bodies, communicating relevant information, and ensuring compliance with existing regulations. 

The Notifying Authority is responsible for receiving applications from conformity assessment bodies, overseeing their designation, and managing their notification processes. It conducts assessments and monitors the activities of these bodies to ensure that they meet the required standards.

In addition to its designation and oversight functions, the Notifying Authority is charged with investigating compliance with specific regulatory articles, such as Article 31, and maintaining communication regarding certifications and the status of notified bodies. Overall, the Notifying Authority plays a crucial role in ensuring that high-risk AI systems adhere to established compliance and conformity assessment processes within the regulatory landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;The notifying authority is responsible for providing the Commission with relevant information regarding notified bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Notifying Authority is the governmental body responsible for overseeing the activities of notified bodies and ensuring compliance with EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_38.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936324</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Body">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Conformity Assessment Body evaluates whether AI systems meet the necessary safety and performance requirements as per regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A Conformity Assessment Body is an organization designated to evaluate and verify compliance with safety standards as mandated by Union harmonisation legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;A conformity assessment body is an organization responsible for assessing the compliance of AI systems based on established requirements and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Conformity Assessment Body is responsible for evaluating compliance with regulations and standards in consultation with the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;A conformity assessment body is an organization that assesses whether products, services, or systems meet specified standards required for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ab1f3b6cbb052c58ff3b9fc75a6d7a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intended Purpose">
      <data key="d0">Intended Purpose</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intended Purpose refers to the specific use for which an AI system is designed by the provider, including context and conditions of use.&lt;SEP&gt;Intended Purpose signifies the specific objectives and applications for which an AI system is designed, influencing its risk assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recall of AI System">
      <data key="d0">Recall of AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recall of AI System refers to actions taken to return or disable an AI system that is no longer compliant with regulations or poses risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Withdrawal of AI System">
      <data key="d0">Withdrawal of AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Withdrawal of AI System indicates actions to prevent an AI system from being available on the market once issues are identified.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance of AI System">
      <data key="d0">Performance of AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance of AI System measures the effectiveness of an AI system in achieving its intended purpose according to set standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment is a comprehensive evaluation process aimed at ensuring that high-risk AI systems comply with established safety and performance standards prior to their deployment. This process is crucial for verifying that these AI systems meet essential regulatory requirements and safety standards necessary for market introduction. Conformity Assessment serves to evaluate compliance of a product, such as an AI system, with relevant regulations as well as specific requirements or standards. It is a regulatory procedure that determines whether a product, service, or process adheres to predefined standards, making it essential for ensuring safety and reliability in the use of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759ef1bca08a56dec0192e47771d9820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_128.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_123.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Body">
      <data key="d0">Notified Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Notified Body is a specific type of Conformity Assessment Body that has been accredited by EU member states to evaluate compliance with relevant regulations, particularly for high-risk categories, including high-risk AI systems. These organizations are responsible for assessing the conformity of various products, processes, or services before they are placed on the market. Notified Bodies play a crucial role in ensuring that these products adhere to regulatory frameworks by issuing certificates confirming compliance with the required standards.

Designated by a member state, a Notified Body is empowered to conduct assessments of certain products or systems to ensure they meet regulatory requirements, as outlined in Article 31. Their responsibilities include not only evaluating conformity but also certifying compliance, especially during instances of suspensions or restrictions.

In summary, Notified Bodies are essential organizations in the regulatory landscape, tasked with the critical function of verifying that products, particularly those classified as high-risk, comply with established regulations before reaching the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified bodies are organizations that are designated to assess conformity and ensure that products meet required regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body is an organization designated by a Member State to assess the conformity of certain products before they can be marketed in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785d0dafc3a62a1aee53267d076b7533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Substantial Modification">
      <data key="d0">Substantial Modification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Substantial Modification refers to any significant change made to an AI system post-market placement that affects compliance or intended use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notifying authority">
      <data key="d0">notifying authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The notifying authority is a national body responsible for managing the assessment, designation, and notification of conformity assessment bodies for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="conformity assessment body">
      <data key="d0">conformity assessment body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A conformity assessment body is responsible for performing tests, certification, and inspections of AI systems to ensure compliance with standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notified body">
      <data key="d0">notified body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A notified body is a specific conformity assessment body that has been approved in accordance with relevant regulations to assess compliance of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body is an organization designated by a member state to assess the conformity of certain products before they can be placed on the market, particularly concerning CE marking.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body refers to an organization designated by national authorities to assess the conformity of products before being placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body is an entity designated to assess the conformity of certain products before they can be marketed in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The notified body is an entity that issues certifications for high-risk AI systems and is responsible for monitoring their compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-595952fa3e7e47cb312adaaad303b73c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="post-market monitoring system">
      <data key="d0">post-market monitoring system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-market monitoring system involves activities by providers to gather feedback from the use of AI systems to ensure their continued compliance and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="market surveillance authority">
      <data key="d0">market surveillance authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance authority refers to the national bodies responsible for enforcing regulatory compliance related to AI practices within Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The market surveillance authority is a national regulatory body dedicated to monitoring compliance with regulations and ensuring the integrity of market activities, particularly concerning high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This organization plays a critical role in overseeing the application and safety of these technologies, utilizing its investigatory powers to conduct thorough inspections and assessments. The authority is specifically tasked with ensuring that operators comply with relevant regulations, including those governing real-time biometric identification systems and other AI technologies.

In addition to its focus on high-risk AI systems, the market surveillance authority monitors broader market practices to ensure adherence to legal standards aimed at consumer protection and safety. This comprehensive oversight is essential for maintaining a fair and safe market environment. The market surveillance authority thus serves as a key player in safeguarding consumer interests while promoting compliance among law enforcement and Union institutions regarding high-risk AI systems testing and related assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935923</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI system">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A high-risk AI system is an artificial intelligence application that poses significant risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights. These systems are subject to stricter compliance requirements due to their potential impact, necessitating adherence to specific regulatory standards to ensure safety and legal compliance. High-risk AI systems are categorized based on their potential effects on health, safety, or fundamental rights, demanding rigorous conformity assessment procedures. Before deployment, these AI technologies must undergo thorough assessments to evaluate their risks and ensure that they meet the established regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are systems that require specific compliance with measures set forth in regulations to ensure data governance and cybersecurity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ffbd2452fab424919d626f5688692d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_122.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CE marking">
      <data key="d0">CE marking</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">CE marking is a certification mark indicating that a product, including an AI system, complies with EU safety standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The CE marking is a certification mark that indicates a product's compliance with European Union regulations relating to health, safety, and environmental protection, required for certain products to be sold in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934345</data>
    </node>
    <node id="conformity assessment activities">
      <data key="d0">conformity assessment activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity assessment activities include testing, certification, and inspection processes to determine if AI systems meet regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="training data">
      <data key="d0">training data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training data is the dataset used to train an AI system, helping it learn and improve its performance by fitting its learnable parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CE Marking">
      <data key="d0">CE Marking</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">CE Marking is a certification mark that signifies a product's compliance with European Union (EU) legislation, specifically concerning health, safety, and environmental protection standards. This certification is essential for the sale of products within the European Economic Area (EEA) and indicates that the products meet the requisite legal requirements for safety, health, and environmental protection. CE Marking ensures that these products adhere to strict regulations, which are designed to safeguard consumers and the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;CE marking is a certification mark that indicates conformity with health, safety, and environmental protection standards for products sold within the European Economic Area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934567</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Standard">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A harmonised standard is a technical specification that has been approved to cover compliance obligations set by the Regulation for AI providers.&lt;SEP&gt;A harmonised standard is a technical standard that has been developed to support EU directives and can be used to demonstrate compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are technical specifications established to ensure compliance with European regulations and directives for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_117.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936000</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Specification">
      <data key="d0">Common Specification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Common specifications provide a set of technical requirements for compliance within various legal frameworks applicable to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training Data">
      <data key="d0">Training Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training data refers to the data used to train AI systems, helping the models learn and adjust their parameters based on input.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data refers to the set of data used to train high-risk AI systems, which affects their performance and potential biases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation Data">
      <data key="d0">Validation Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Validation data assesses the performance of an AI system, ensuring it adapts and prevents issues like underfitting or overfitting during training.&lt;SEP&gt;Validation data refers to data used for evaluating and tuning the performance of an AI system, preventing issues such as underfitting or overfitting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Data">
      <data key="d0">Testing Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing data is a type of data utilized for the independent evaluation of AI systems prior to their market release.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing data is utilized to independently evaluate the performance of an AI system before it is made available for public use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Input Data">
      <data key="d0">Input Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Input data comprises the information entered into an AI system for processing, subject to legal acquisition standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data encompasses data acquired or provided to an AI system, which is essential for generating the system's output.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data refers to the information that an AI system receives or acquires to generate outputs or make decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data is the information fed into high-risk AI systems, which must be relevant and sufficiently representative for their intended purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data refers to the information fed into high-risk AI systems that are processed and analyzed to generate outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Data">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric Data encompasses various types of personal information derived from physical characteristics, such as fingerprints, facial recognition, and iris scans, which are used for identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric Data refers to personal information derived from unique physical or behavioral characteristics of individuals, which are utilized primarily for identification and verification purposes, particularly in law enforcement settings. This data encompasses distinct traits such as fingerprints and facial recognition data, which can be quantified and measured through various technical processes and surveillance technologies. 

Additionally, biometric data includes biological measurements or statistics that can be analyzed to infer the emotional states of individuals. It is essential for confirming identities and plays a critical role in security and identification protocols. Biometric data is classified as sensitive personal data due to the unique personal attributes it encompasses, making it a vital tool in the categorization and identification of individuals. Overall, biometric data serves both identification and emotional recognition functions, enhancing the authentication processes used in various settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data includes physiological and behavioral characteristics used to identify emotions, such as facial expressions and voice modulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric Data refers to the physical, physiological, and behavioral characteristics used for establishing individual identities.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data includes personal information such as fingerprints, facial recognition, and other unique identifiers that can be processed by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1a48b7c6d78e001878383cb0acaf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-737358b61293029e1a6d7326160654fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
