    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2016/679 refers to the General Data Protection Regulation which provides guidelines for the collection and processing of personal information of individuals within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679, commonly referred to as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), is a comprehensive legal framework established by the European Union to enhance the protection of personal data and privacy rights for individuals within the EU. This regulation governs data protection and privacy, specifically focusing on data processing activities conducted both inside and outside the EU that affect EU residents.

The GDPR sets forth stringent guidelines and obligations related to the collection and processing of personal information, including those pertaining to sensitive data types such as biometric data and data processing in high-risk contexts, including law enforcement. It introduces the concept that AI systems which involve profiling may be classified as high-risk, requiring enhanced data protection measures.

Overall, Regulation (EU) 2016/679 represents a significant advancement in the realm of data protection and privacy, providing a robust framework aimed at safeguarding individuals' fundamental rights in the context of data processing. Its implementation underscores the necessity for stringent controls and obligations to ensure that individuals’ privacy rights are respected and upheld across the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679, known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), sets guidelines for the collection and processing of personal data, including specific protections for biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679, also known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), is a comprehensive data protection law aimed at enhancing individual rights regarding their personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679, known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), aims to protect personal data and ensure free movement of such data within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb</data>
