    <node id="Directive (EU) 2022/2557">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2022/2557</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2022/2557 addresses the resilience of critical entities and the necessary measures for the identification of perpetrators in various criminal offenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2022/2557 is a legislative document that provides guidelines on the protection of individuals' interests within the EU context.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2022/2557 is a regulation detailing the standards for critical infrastructure protection and associated threats to public safety.&lt;SEP&gt;This directive pertains to the resilience of critical entities, replacing an older directive and focusing on enhancing security measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2022/2557 is a regulation concerning the management and operation of critical infrastructure in the European Union, particularly in relation to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec6a8294e2a2ad2569029d260c4d7673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6badc71855b10bbd17a31c7dfef0c442&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI model">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI model is a versatile and advanced artificial intelligence system designed to perform a diverse range of tasks across various applications. These models are subject to compliance evaluations and assessments to identify potential systemic risks associated with their deployment. When marketed within the European Union, they must adhere to regulatory oversight to ensure their safe integration into society. Due to their capabilities and impacts, general-purpose AI models require ongoing monitoring for systemic risks, which are evaluated based on specific thresholds. Overall, they represent a significant technological advancement with both broad utility and important considerations for their governance and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are artificial intelligence systems designed for various applications, which can present systemic risks depending on their impact capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are AI systems designed for diverse applications and subjected to regulatory scrutiny by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0c14a128bfd78c4c5056f7102cc152&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935917</data>
    </node>
