    <node id="High-Impact Capabilities">
      <data key="d0">High-Impact Capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-impact capabilities refer to the advanced abilities of general-purpose AI models that can significantly affect various sectors or society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Risk">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic Risk encompasses the potential dangers and hazards posed by AI models and technologies that could lead to widespread harm across various sectors, including public health, safety, and fundamental rights. This type of risk is characterized by the possibility of collapse or failure of entire systems or markets, particularly in relation to the impact of AI at the Union level. Systemic Risk is associated with the interconnected nature of systems and entities, suggesting that failure in one component could trigger significant consequences throughout the broader financial system or society. It highlights the need for systematic management according to regulatory standards to mitigate threats that could disrupt the stability and functioning of larger systems within which these general-purpose AI models operate. Overall, Systemic Risk refers to the significant potential for widespread adverse effects stemming from high-impact AI capabilities and their influence on societal structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to the potential for a significant disruption in the entire system due to specific entities or factors, particularly in relation to AI models and their compliance obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to the potential for widespread failures or negative impacts resulting from the performance of general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-212b902a4529db42951674775ac3ec73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0c14a128bfd78c4c5056f7102cc152</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Downstream Provider">
      <data key="d0">Downstream Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A downstream provider integrates AI models, either on their own or through contractual relations, to deliver AI systems to end-users.&lt;SEP&gt;Downstream Provider is an entity that provides an AI system that integrates AI models, with potential contractual relations involved in its operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Downstream Provider is any entity that integrates or utilizes AI systems for content creation and is accountable for compliance with regulations regarding AI technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Market">
      <data key="d0">Union Market</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Market refers to the collective economic and regulatory marketplace within the jurisdiction of the European Union, where artificial intelligence (AI) systems are made available for use. It encompasses a space influenced by digital and technological changes, emphasizing compliance with a range of specific regulations, particularly for high-risk AI systems. This marketplace prioritizes innovations from small and medium-sized enterprises, including start-ups, ensuring they adhere to necessary legislative requirements aimed at safeguarding public safety and interests.

Furthermore, compliance with copyright laws is essential for AI model providers operating within the Union Market. Overall, the Union Market serves as a critical platform for the deployment of AI technologies, balancing innovation with regulation to maintain standards and protect consumers throughout the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union market represents the economic landscape within the European Union where products, including AI systems, are marketed, emphasizing competitiveness and innovation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Impact">
      <data key="d0">Market Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Impact denotes the effects that AI technologies have on various aspects of the economy and society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Model">
      <data key="d0">AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Model refers to a general-purpose artificial intelligence system that serves multiple functions and can be integrated into various other AI systems. It is a computational construct specifically designed to perform distinct tasks using artificial intelligence technologies, enabling it to make decisions and solve problems based on data and algorithms. The AI Model possesses varying levels of complexity and capability, which may introduce identifiable risks at the Union level depending on its implementation. This model encompasses various techniques applicable for tasks such as content generation and semantic interpretation. Overall, an AI Model is a comprehensive computational framework designed to execute functions typically requiring human intelligence, while also acknowledging the potential systemic risks associated with its capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935636</data>
    </node>
