      <data key="d5">1783936075</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charter of Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Charter of Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charter of Fundamental Rights is a document that outlines essential rights guaranteed to individuals in the EU, impacting the implementation of laws, including those regarding AI.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union outlines various rights, including the right to vote, which is a fundamental democratic principle.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bedecbbbba0ded6846e6dc97756b7de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_62.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Procedural Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Procedural Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Procedural Fundamental Rights refer to legal rights ensuring fair processes in legal matters, which can be threatened by improper use of AI technologies in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tax and Customs Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Tax and Customs Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax and Customs Authorities are governmental bodies responsible for implementing tax laws and trade regulations, occasionally using AI for administrative functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Intelligence Units">
      <data key="d0">Financial Intelligence Units</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Intelligence Units are specialized agencies that analyze financial data to combat economic crimes, such as money laundering, and may utilize AI technologies in their operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial intelligence units are entities tasked with carrying out administrative tasks and analyzing information as per Union law on anti-money laundering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Union Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Institutions are bodies that work together to establish regulations and cooperatively ensure compliance and safety in various sectors, including product safety and financial services.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Institutions comprise various bodies within the European Union that enact policies and laws concerning member states, including regulations on AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Institutions refer to the various agencies and bodies of the European Union responsible for implementing policies and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Institutions refer to various bodies and agencies within the European Union that are responsible for a range of legislative, enforcement, and oversight functions. Key entities within these institutions include the European Parliament and the Council of the European Union, alongside other offices and agencies. These institutions operate under the guidance of the European Data Protection Supervisor, particularly concerning regulations associated with artificial intelligence (AI). 

Union Institutions may implement AI systems to enhance law enforcement efforts, aiding in crime prevention and investigation. They are also subject to compliance with data protection regulations, facing administrative fines for non-compliance. Furthermore, Union Institutions are involved in governance and regulation across the European Union, which includes the oversight of market surveillance and adherence to EU law.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions refer to bodies, offices, or agencies involved in the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Person Victim">
      <data key="d0">Natural Person Victim</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural persons may become victims of criminal offences, and their risks are assessed using specific AI tools designed for law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601</data>
