    </node>
    <node id="court">
      <data key="d0">court</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Court refers to the judicial setting where legal cases are adjudicated, and outcomes are determined.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7110d3511298db6faf629e1d559dc5ba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Authorities are government entities responsible for implementing and regulating the use of high-risk AI systems within their jurisdiction.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Authorities are governmental bodies tasked with administering essential public services, such as healthcare and social security benefits. They play a crucial role in interacting with small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and start-ups, offering guidance on compliance with relevant regulations. In addition to these responsibilities, Public Authorities are also required to manage high-risk AI systems, adhering to specific regulations governing their operation. These entities must ensure compliance with the Regulation on High-Risk AI Systems by a designated deadline, which involves registering AI systems as mandated by EU law. Furthermore, Public Authorities are responsible for implementing policies and regulations, enforcing compliance, and overseeing the deployment of AI systems within their jurisdiction.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Authorities are governmental entities that may act in collaboration with the European Union under specific international agreements for law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Assistance Benefits">
      <data key="d0">Public Assistance Benefits</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Assistance Benefits include essential services such as healthcare, social security, and social services aimed at supporting vulnerable individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934177</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Resources">
      <data key="d0">Financial Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Resources refer to assets like housing, electricity, and telecommunications that individuals may access or be denied based on AI evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial resources encompass essentials like housing, electricity, and telecommunication services that are often accessed based on credit evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-431ae031d4ead528e84df75526b0f1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934177</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulation">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Regulation encompasses governance frameworks intended to ensure the safe and compliant use of AI systems, especially regarding personal impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulation refers to the rules and requirements that govern the development, deployment, and use of artificial intelligence models and systems in the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulation refers to the framework established to govern the development and use of artificial intelligence technologies within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulation refers to the legal frameworks and guidelines that govern the development and deployment of AI systems, ensuring their compliance with safety and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulation refers to the legal framework established to govern the development and application of Artificial Intelligence technologies within the EU, ensuring compliance with Union standards and ethical guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936007</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Healthcare Services">
      <data key="d0">Healthcare Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Healthcare Services refer to essential medical services provided to natural persons, often available through public assistance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934177</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social Security Benefits">
      <data key="d0">Social Security Benefits</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Social Security Benefits are government-provided financial benefits that support individuals during times of need such as maternity, illness, or old age.</data>
