    <node id="Conformity Assessment Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Procedure is the process of verifying that AI systems comply with relevant regulations and standards prior to deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Conformity Assessment Procedure is a defined guideline under the regulation that stipulates how products must be evaluated for compliance with cybersecurity standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Conformity Assessment Procedure is a formal and systematic process designed to evaluate whether high-risk AI systems comply with established safety standards and regulatory requirements. This procedure involves various methods aimed at verifying that these AI systems meet the necessary legal requirements before they can be marketed or deployed. Specifically, the conformity assessment ensures that high-risk products fulfill specified standards and regulations, thereby safeguarding public safety and ensuring adherence to relevant legal acts. Overall, the Conformity Assessment Procedure is essential for maintaining compliance and fostering trust in high-risk AI technologies.</data>
