    <node id="Annex III">
      <data key="d0">Annex III</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex III is a crucial component of regulatory documents pertaining to artificial intelligence (AI) systems within the European Union (EU). It encompasses a classification of high-risk AI systems that are subject to specific regulations and oversight, particularly due to their potential impact on safety and fundamental rights. The annex provides a comprehensive framework for regulatory oversight, detailing the criteria for classifying various types of high-risk AI systems, including those utilized by financial institutions that necessitate enhanced scrutiny.

The descriptions highlight that Annex III includes a list of specific AI systems that require regulation, emphasizing the serious risks these high-risk systems pose to multiple Member States. It aims to ensure a harmonized approach to regulation across the EU by outlining detailed standards for risk evaluation. Furthermore, the annex delineates the regulatory requirements embedded in the legal frameworks and specifies the conditions that determine whether an AI system is categorized as high-risk.

Annex III is closely associated with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, which addresses the necessary protocols and standards for high-risk AI systems, necessitating careful evaluation and oversight to safeguard public interests. It features area headings for AI systems that require assessment or evaluation and is subject to annual reviews for potential amendments by the Commission. Overall, Annex III plays an essential role in establishing regulatory obligations and conformity assessment procedures for the deployment of high-risk AI systems within the regulatory framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex III outlines the provisions and requirements for high-risk AI systems in relation to testing and regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex III refers to a specific section of regulations that outlines the requirements for testing high-risk AI systems in various areas, including law enforcement and migration.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex III outlines the specific AI systems that have a maximum certificate validity period of four years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe49d95d50900e82a706b2766339562f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
