    </node>
    <node id="Technical Solutions">
      <data key="d0">Technical Solutions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Solutions are the methods and technologies available to correct or mitigate adverse impacts caused by AI systems, focusing on health, safety, and rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical Solutions refer to methodologies or technologies available to correct or reverse harmful outcomes produced by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions are methods required for marking and detecting AI-generated content to differentiate it from human-generated content.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions refer to methods and tools used to ensure AI systems are effective, reliable, and comply with standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions encompass the tools and methods used to facilitate the development and implementation of AI technologies in an ethical and efficient manner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe49d95d50900e82a706b2766339562f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936187</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harm">
      <data key="d0">Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harm refers to the potential negative effects that arise from the deployment of AI systems, impacting individuals or groups either physically or psychologically.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adverse Impact">
      <data key="d0">Adverse Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Adverse Impact represents the unintended negative consequences that may arise from AI system outputs, particularly on vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dependence on AI Outcomes">
      <data key="d0">Dependence on AI Outcomes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Dependence on AI Outcomes refers to the degree to which individuals and groups rely on decisions made by AI systems, which can pose risks to their rights and interests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Delegated Acts">
      <data key="d0">Delegated Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Delegated Acts are legal instruments that allow the Commission to amend regulations, including criteria regarding systemic risks associated with AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated Acts are regulatory measures that the Commission can adopt to amend existing laws regarding high-risk AI systems based on evolving understandings or assessments of risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated Acts denote the legal provisions enabling the Commission to implement amendments and updates to existing regulations related to AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated acts are legal acts of the EU that enable the European Commission to supplement or amend non-essential parts of legally binding Union acts.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated acts are powers granted to the Commission to amend specific annexes and regulations relating to AI compliance as technology evolves.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935597</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Commission">
      <data key="d0">The Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission is a governing body within the European Union, vested with multiple responsibilities related to the regulation and implementation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Acting as the executive branch of the EU, the Commission plays a crucial role in developing guidelines and regulatory frameworks related to AI, including the establishment of an AI regulatory sandbox. Its functions encompass proposing legislation, enforcing laws, and managing various administrative tasks aimed at ensuring compliant AI practices.

In addition to its legislative responsibilities, the Commission actively engages in consultations with Member States to address any objections concerning assessments and authorizations related to AI technologies. The Commission oversees the designation of Union AI Testing Support Structures and is tasked with adopting guidelines and delegated acts pertinent to AI regulations, ensuring that safety standards are maintained within the AI landscape.

Furthermore, the Commission is responsible for coordinating and ensuring cooperation among notified bodies concerning high-risk AI systems and compliance procedures. As an authoritative body with exclusive powers, it supervises and enforces specific regulations under the Treaties, safeguarding various interests, including public security and confidentiality. Through its efforts, the Commission aims to enhance the governance surrounding AI, aligning it with EU policies and promoting responsible innovation in this evolving field.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission refers to the European Commission, which is in charge of issuing requests for standardisation and ensuring regulatory compliance in various sectors including AI.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission refers to an authoritative body that can impose fines on providers of general-purpose AI models for regulatory non-compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is an entity that may develop initiatives to facilitate the lowering of technical barriers for AI development and promote cross-border data exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is responsible for investigating the competence of notified bodies and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a811acaf13b6420a717f6aa21a6ed331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_165.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Autonomous Robots">
      <data key="d0">Autonomous Robots</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Autonomous robots are increasingly capable machines designed for various roles in manufacturing, personal assistance, and care, requiring safety in operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18cf1aa30864348514b20fe64038fba8</data>
