    </node>
    <node id="Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Surveillance involves monitoring individuals or groups, often through technologies, to gather information, typically for security or law enforcement purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data protection refers to the process of safeguarding personal data from misuse or unauthorized access, as mandated by various regulations and laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Notified Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Notified Bodies are accredited organizations established under national law in EU Member States, playing a vital role in assessing the conformity of high-risk AI systems and certain products against specific regulatory requirements. Designated by national authorities, these organizations are crucial for ensuring that high-risk AI systems comply with relevant regulations and standards. Emphasizing independence, objectivity, and impartiality in their assessment activities, Notified Bodies are dedicated to safeguarding confidentiality and professionalism throughout the evaluation process.

These entities assist providers in meeting regulatory standards by verifying that high-risk AI systems and other products meet necessary criteria for safety and effectiveness before being introduced to the market. Notified Bodies possess legal personality and are committed to conducting thorough conformity assessment activities within their respective fields. Moreover, they ensure that any subcontractors or subsidiaries adhere to the same regulatory requirements.

In summary, Notified Bodies are essential organizations responsible for maintaining safety and regulatory compliance for high-risk AI systems and various products within the EU market. They serve as designated entities responsible for conducting conformity assessments and certifying that products or systems meet established regulatory standards, thereby ensuring compliance with EU quality management system standards and technical documentation requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a57bbcc3ccf00f26352f12c36036aedf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a310ed4ba9b96c860daae9a944f07fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_145.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_125.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936324</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member State">
      <data key="d0">Member State</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A Member State refers to a country that is a part of the European Union (EU) and is integral to the governing body of the union. These Member States are bound by specific regulations and authority protocols that guide their designation, certification, and overarching compliance with EU standards, particularly in sectors involving biometric technologies and high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems.

Each Member State is responsible for ensuring adherence to EU regulations by establishing national laws and implementing effective conformity assessment procedures. This includes creating mechanisms for market surveillance that uphold the regulatory framework set by the EU, thus ensuring compliance and safety in AI systems. Member States not only play a crucial role in legislative discussions but also actively participate in the EU's broader political and economic framework.

In addition to their regulatory and compliance responsibilities, Member States determine and provide necessary language and comprehension requirements for AI instructions, thereby establishing standards for language accessibility in AI deployments. As part of their enforcement duties, they also possess the authority to impose administrative fines to ensure compliance.

In summary, Member States are sovereign entities within the European Union that are vital to the implementation and oversight of EU mandates, focusing particularly on emerging technologies and AI systems. They oversee conformity assessment bodies and enforce testing regulations as stipulated by Union legislation, reinforcing their essential role in the collective governance of the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States are countries within a union that notify and regulate the competence of notified bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;A Member State refers to countries that are members of the European Union and adhere to its regulations regarding AI systems certification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936246</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Activities">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Activities are processes conducted by notified bodies to verify and ensure that products, services, or organizations meet the necessary standards and regulations across various sectors. These activities encompass a series of procedures and evaluations that are crucial in determining compliance with established guidelines, particularly for high-risk AI systems. The aim of Conformity Assessment Activities is to assess compliance before certifying products, ensuring that they adhere to the requisite standards and regulations. Through these systematic evaluations, conformity assessment activities play a pivotal role in maintaining safety and regulatory compliance within the marketplace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Personality">
      <data key="d0">Legal Personality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal personality refers to the recognition of an organization as a distinct legal entity capable of owning property and being liable for its actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Quality management requirements are standards and practices that notified bodies must fulfill to ensure effective and reliable conformity assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Resource Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Resource Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Resource requirements encompass the necessary tools, personnel, and infrastructure that notified bodies need to effectively conduct conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity Requirements are standards that products with digital elements, particularly high-risk AI systems, must meet to ensure their resilience and safety against cyber threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity requirements entail measures that notified bodies must implement to protect sensitive information during conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934966</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independence">
      <data key="d0">Independence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Independence refers to the need for notified bodies to operate without influence from external parties that may compromise their assessment integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Impartiality">
      <data key="d0">Impartiality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Impartiality signifies the objective and fair conduct of notified bodies during conformity assessments, ensuring unbiased evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Liability Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Liability Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Liability Insurance is coverage that protects notified bodies against claims related to their conformity assessment activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Liability insurance is a requirement for notified bodies to mitigate risks associated with the consequences of their assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 78">
      <data key="d0">Article 78</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 78 establishes specific confidentiality obligations concerning information and documentation obtained during compliance assessments, particularly as they relate to conformity assessment activities. This legal provision ensures that personnel in notified bodies adhere to proper conduct and maintain confidentiality regarding sensitive information. Article 78 also outlines the confidentiality requirements for information acquired by national public authorities under Union law, including details pertinent to high-risk AI systems. Additionally, it specifies the legal elements or requirements that take effect on a predetermined date, reinforcing the importance of safeguarding confidential information in compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 78 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 pertains to the confidentiality of information obtained during the regulatory compliance process.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 78 pertains to the confidentiality of sensitive information during investigations conducted by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 78 refers to a specific provision within EU legislation that mandates confidentiality for information obtained by notified bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a310ed4ba9b96c860daae9a944f07fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8512760339eb776d946a91a28089b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Standardisation Organisations">
      <data key="d0">European Standardisation Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">European Standardisation Organisations are bodies that develop and maintain standards and facilitate coordination among notified bodies regarding assessment activities.&lt;SEP&gt;European Standardisation Organisations are bodies that work towards the development and dissemination of standards across Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;European standardisation organisations develop harmonised standards for various requirements as part of EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;European Standardisation Organisations are groups tasked with developing and promoting harmonised standards within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;European standardisation organisations are responsible for developing and implementing standards within the EU framework, particularly for AI systems and models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Personnel refers to the individuals who perform various roles within an organization or system, often requiring specific expertise.&lt;SEP&gt;Personnel refers to the staff and workforce associated with notified bodies, responsible for carrying out conformity assessment tasks and maintaining professional integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competence">
      <data key="d0">Competence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Competence pertains to the required skills, knowledge, and authority for individuals assigned to implement AI system instructions and conduct oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Competence refers to the requisite skills and expertise that notified bodies and personnel must possess to effectively evaluate conformity assessments and AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_91.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934927</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Technical Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Personnel are individuals with specialized knowledge and skills required to conduct evaluations and assessments in conformity assessment activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Scientific Personnel are individuals involved in providing scientific expertise and support for the evaluation of AI systems and data computing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Legal Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Personnel are individuals with legal expertise who ensure compliance with regulations and handle legal responsibilities in conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 2 outlines specific requirements that high-risk AI systems must comply with to ensure their safe deployment and use.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 2 refers to a part of the regulation that establishes the requirements that high-risk AI systems must meet for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 2 refers to a specific part of regulatory text that outlines particular compliance requirements to be adhered to by providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 2 refers to a specific part of the regulatory framework established by the European Union, which outlines the necessary requirements that high-risk AI systems must comply with to ensure their safety, efficacy, and conformity. It emphasizes the importance of a conformity assessment process, detailing the standards that such AI systems must meet to be deemed compliant and safe for the market. Additionally, Section 2 addresses requirements related to standardization processes within the EU, ensuring that high-risk AI systems adhere to established guidelines and criteria for their deployment. Overall, this section serves as a critical component of the regulatory framework aimed at regulating high-risk AI technologies effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c17bf6e803eec807c9fc7299d71d51d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">High-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems are designed for applications that require human oversight to ensure they function correctly and mitigate negative consequences.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to artificial intelligence applications that necessitate compliance with EU regulations due to their potential impact on safety and health, requiring specific certification.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to artificial intelligence systems that require stringent design and development protocols to ensure accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity throughout their lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936012</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stakeholders and Organisations">
      <data key="d0">Stakeholders and Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholders and organizations include metrology and benchmarking authorities involved in the measurement and assessment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Metrics">
      <data key="d0">Performance Metrics</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance metrics are measurements that gauge the accuracy and robustness of high-risk AI systems, crucial for their validation and operational use.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance metrics are standards outlined in Article 15 to evaluate the accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935672</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Feedback Loops">
      <data key="d0">Feedback Loops</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Feedback loops are processes where outputs from AI systems influence future inputs to improve operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops involve processes through which inputs are refined and adjusted based on outputs, requiring monitoring and mitigation strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops refer to the processes by which the output of a high-risk AI system is used to influence future inputs, which must be managed to avoid biased outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops occur when outputs from AI systems influence future inputs, potentially creating cycles of discrimination or bias if not managed correctly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934740</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Redundancy Solutions">
      <data key="d0">Technical Redundancy Solutions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical redundancy solutions involve backup systems and fail-safe plans that enhance the resilience of high-risk AI systems against errors and faults.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unauthorized Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Unauthorized Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Unauthorized third parties refer to individuals or groups attempting to exploit vulnerabilities in AI systems for malicious intents.&lt;SEP&gt;Unauthorized third parties represent individuals or entities attempting to exploit vulnerabilities in high-risk AI systems, posing a cybersecurity risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Measures">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity Measures are protections put in place to safeguard information and data integrity against unauthorized access or breaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity measures are strategies and practices implemented to protect high-risk AI systems from attacks and unauthorized alterations.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity measures include techniques and strategies implemented to defend against unauthorized access and attacks on AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity Measures are protocols and practices designed to protect data from theft and damage, particularly in the context of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d7d6f2dd7e28584da10fdb340b37fd0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935578</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Poisoning">
      <data key="d0">Data Poisoning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data poisoning is a type of attack where malicious data is introduced to a training set to corrupt the learning process of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Data poisoning refers to attacks that introduce corrupt data into training datasets to manipulate AI outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Data poisoning refers to attacks that manipulate the training data sets of AI systems, affecting their performance and integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5765a06abb615496a937c9303e1583cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Poisoning">
      <data key="d0">Model Poisoning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model poisoning involves attacks targeting pre-trained components of AI systems, potentially compromising their reliability and outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Model poisoning is a vulnerability where business-critical models are compromised by corrupt components used during AI training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Examples">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Examples</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Adversarial examples are inputs designed to deceive an AI model, resulting in incorrect outputs and demonstrating vulnerability.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial examples are malicious inputs specifically designed to deceive AI models into making incorrect predictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity refers to the comprehensive set of practices, measures, and technologies designed to protect computer systems, networks, and data from unauthorized access, attacks, and potential threats. In the context of artificial intelligence (AI), cybersecurity is especially critical as it focuses on safeguarding high-risk AI systems from unauthorized access and actions that could compromise their integrity, confidentiality, and availability. This includes protecting hardware, software, and data from theft or damage, as well as preventing disruptions in service. Overall, cybersecurity encompasses a range of strategies aimed at defending against digital attacks, thereby ensuring the secure operation of systems and services, particularly those involving artificial intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d7d6f2dd7e28584da10fdb340b37fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5765a06abb615496a937c9303e1583cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="System Vulnerabilities">
      <data key="d0">System Vulnerabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">System vulnerabilities are weaknesses in AI systems that may be exploited unless properly addressed, impacting their performance and security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Public Authorities are government bodies responsible for enforcing laws and regulations, including those related to the protection of fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;National Public Authorities are relevant bodies that cooperate with the Market Surveillance Authority in evaluating AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National public authorities are government bodies that handle various regulatory responsibilities, including receiving notifications regarding serious incidents in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National public authorities are governmental bodies responsible for supervising compliance with Union law regarding fundamental rights, including the regulation of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935039</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant National Public Authorities or Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Relevant National Public Authorities or Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">These authorities assist the Market Surveillance Authority in evaluating AI systems, ensuring public safety and compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Corrective Actions">
      <data key="d0">Corrective Actions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Corrective actions are measures taken by providers to ensure compliance of high-risk AI systems, including withdrawal and recall of non-compliant systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Corrective actions refer to measures mandated by regulatory bodies to ensure AI systems comply with regulations, such as market withdrawal or recall.&lt;SEP&gt;Corrective actions refer to the measures that must be taken to ensure compliance of high-risk AI systems with established safety requirements and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934473</data>
    </node>
    <node id="operator">
      <data key="d0">operator</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The operator is any entity responsible for making AI systems available on the market and ensuring compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 18">
      <data key="d0">Article 18</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 18 is a specific section of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 that addresses corrective measures for non-compliance of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 18 pertains to the documentation that must be kept by providers to demonstrate compliance of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 18 refers to a specific section of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 that addresses the application of provisions relevant to general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8affbc363cca00e716c4494cb81a558a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_94.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935993</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paragraph 2">
      <data key="d0">paragraph 2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraph 2 refers to a specific section within the regulations that stipulates the time frame operators must adhere to for corrective actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="harmonised standards">
      <data key="d0">harmonised standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonised standards are established guidelines that AI systems must comply with to ensure market conformity within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are technical specifications established by standardisation bodies to facilitate compliance with regulations in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are technical specifications that facilitate compliance and regulatory adherence for AI systems within the EU framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6fc829d58f1a7bbf3defd5cbe758b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935923</data>
    </node>
    <node id="non-compliance">
      <data key="d0">non-compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-compliance encompasses instances where products or systems fail to meet established regulatory requirements or safety standards as outlined by the relevant authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-compliance refers to situations where an AI system does not meet regulatory requirements, necessitating corrective actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Compliant AI System">
      <data key="d0">Non-Compliant AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-Compliant AI Systems refer to AI technologies that fail to meet established regulatory standards and may pose risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 5">
      <data key="d0">Article 5</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 5 is a key provision within the AI Systems Regulation in the European Union that defines and establishes a comprehensive list of prohibited practices related to the deployment and management of AI systems. It specifically outlines certain AI practices that are deemed unsafe or unethical, which AI systems must comply with to ensure their responsible use. The article emphasizes the importance of adhering to specific provisions that delineate these prohibitions in the context of AI development and application. Additionally, Article 5 includes provisions for the European Commission to evaluate and implement necessary updates to the list of prohibited practices, ensuring that regulations remain relevant and effective in managing the evolving landscape of artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5 refers to provisions within the regulatory framework that establish prohibitions and restrictions regarding the usage of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5 specifies prohibitions on certain AI practices, forming a core part of the regulations governing AI usage in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935923</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 50">
      <data key="d0">Article 50</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 50 details the transparency obligations laid down in the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 specifies compliance requirements and obligations for the oversight of AI systems within the legal framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 specifies the requirements for additional transparency measures concerning certain categories of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 refers to a specific provision within the Regulation that pertains to the deployment of high-risk AI systems in relation to natural persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notification">
      <data key="d0">Notification</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Notification refers to the procedure wherein the provider must inform the Commission that a general-purpose AI model meets the regulatory criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Notification refers to the process by which market surveillance authorities inform the relevant entities about measures regarding product compliance and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935597</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provisional Measure">
      <data key="d0">Provisional Measure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Provisional Measure is a temporary action taken by market surveillance authorities in response to compliance issues related to products, particularly in the context of AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation of AI Practices">
      <data key="d0">Regulation of AI Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Regulation of AI Practices refers to specific legal provisions governing the use and compliance of AI technologies to ensure safety and ethical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934207</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-Time Systems">
      <data key="d0">Real-Time Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-Time Systems refer to systems that operate without significant delay, utilizing live or near-live data for analysis and processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time systems process biometric data instantly or with minimal delay, usually utilizing live material like video to identify individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d1a48b7c6d78e001878383cb0acaf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_17.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934208</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post Systems">
      <data key="d0">Post Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post Systems are systems that involve biometric data captured and processed after a significant delay, using previously generated material like video footage.&lt;SEP&gt;Post systems refer to technologies that identify individuals based on biometric data captured earlier, allowing for significant delays in comparison processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d1a48b7c6d78e001878383cb0acaf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_17.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934208</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reference Database">
      <data key="d0">Reference Database</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference database is a collection of recorded biometric data against which new data can be compared for identification of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The reference database is a repository against which input data is checked for validity and accuracy in high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_17.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Surveillance Technology">
      <data key="d0">Surveillance Technology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Surveillance Technology encompasses devices and systems used to monitor individuals or environments, typically involving cameras and biometric systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d1a48b7c6d78e001878383cb0acaf58</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_17.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934208</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers">
      <data key="d0">Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are entities or individuals pivotal in the development, supply, and implementation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and services across various applications. They play a critical role in the AI value chain, ensuring access to high-quality data necessary for the development and validation of high-risk AI technologies. Providers can include companies as well as individual developers, and they are responsible for navigating a complex landscape of applicable laws and regulations, particularly concerning high-risk AI technologies and intellectual property rights.

In their efforts to comply with these regulations, Providers create and maintain post-market monitoring systems to oversee the performance and safety of their AI technologies. This ongoing oversight involves reporting incidents and notifying regulatory authorities about their testing processes. Providers also participate in AI regulatory sandboxes, which allow them to test compliance and engage in innovative practices within a controlled environment, thereby helping to meet safety and performance standards.

When offering General-Purpose AI Models, Providers may seek reassessment from regulatory bodies to determine the risk designation of their models. They must ensure that any modifications to their products remain compliant with established regulations. Furthermore, Providers are responsible for preparing and supplying necessary documentation and instructions related to their AI products, emphasizing the importance of regulatory adherence to avoid potential penalties.

Overall, Providers are essential to the regulatory framework surrounding AI technologies, working diligently to foster safe, compliant, and innovative AI systems. They are particularly dedicated to the development and management of AI systems that interact with natural persons and ensure compliance with Union harmonization legislation and regulations. Ultimately, the activities of Providers directly impact how AI technologies are delivered and managed in a rapidly evolving market landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc29985a43f3bd521b3a1c9eb9ba756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_145.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are entities responsible for using high-risk AI systems, accountable for ensuring compliance with usage instructions and monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are entities that are responsible for the implementation and operation of products or technologies, particularly high-risk AI systems. These can be organizations or individuals who deploy such systems in their operations within the Union. As Deployers, they are subject to regulatory compliance concerning both market and safety regulations. They play a crucial role in ensuring the effective use of AI systems while also being obligated to report any associated risks. Overall, Deployers are tasked with not only deploying these technologies but also with adhering to applicable regulations to ensure safe and responsible use.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are individuals or organizations that implement high-risk AI systems and require appropriate training and instructions to use them effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are organizations or individuals responsible for the implementation and management of AI systems, ensuring they meet regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are the individuals or organizations responsible for implementing high-risk AI systems and must ensure adherence to relevant standards and guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2edb4e37d5b6a1ec68d071ea273b4e52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
