    <node id="Board">
      <data key="d0">Board</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Board is a comprehensive governing body integral to the oversight and implementation of regulations related to artificial intelligence (AI) within the European Union. Its primary function is advisory, as it provides input and guidance during the standardization process and aids the Commission in establishing guidelines for AI systems. The Board collaborates closely with the AI Office to ensure that the codes of practice comply with obligations and objectives outlined in various regulatory articles.

In its advisory capacity, the Board coordinates and promotes cooperation among national competent authorities regarding the operation of AI regulatory sandboxes. It represents diverse interests within the AI ecosystem, facilitating the effective implementation of AI regulations through various advisory tasks. The Board possesses the authority to form both standing and temporary sub-groups to delve into specific regulatory issues, allowing for detailed discussions and informed decisions on complex matters.

Furthermore, the Board participates in decision-making processes related to market surveillance, empowered to formally request actions from the AI Office to implement the regulatory framework. It also oversees communications concerning penalties imposed under AI regulations, receiving information on these fines as part of its regulatory oversight responsibilities.

In addition to its regulatory functions, the Board offers guidance and support to small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and start-ups, helping them navigate compliance with regulations. This effort ensures that the safety and interests of the AI ecosystem are upheld while assisting national authorities in their implementation tasks. Overall, the multifaceted role of the Board is vital in shaping a balanced and effective regulatory landscape for AI, ensuring adherence to established procedures and the impartial operation of its activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d8b1632746db5110bcd9632c1ace58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacbea1ddddc58fbf14c882b36d9a6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_161.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_149.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="market surveillance authorities">
      <data key="d0">market surveillance authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance authorities are entities responsible for evaluating compliance of AI systems and ensuring adherence to regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing compliance with laws and regulations in the marketplace.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are regulatory entities tasked with ensuring compliance with regulations and standards within various markets, particularly focusing on product safety and quality. They play a crucial role in overseeing market practices by conducting joint investigations and monitoring adherence to relevant laws. These authorities are responsible for making sure that both products and high-risk AI systems meet the necessary safety standards and regulatory requirements. In essence, market surveillance authorities are integral to promoting fair market practices and protecting consumers by enforcing compliance with established market regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacbea1ddddc58fbf14c882b36d9a6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_149.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json</data>
