    <node id="commercial service">
      <data key="d0">commercial service</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Commercial service refers to the primary service provided by platforms that may use biometric categorisation as an ancillary feature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac04e8bc9dd9ff3998ce3c08f3800f57</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934220</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-purpose AI systems">
      <data key="d0">General-purpose AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI systems refer to artificial intelligence systems designed for a wide range of applications, which may be classified as high-risk depending on their use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_85.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934221</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Value Chain">
      <data key="d0">AI Value Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Value Chain refers to the series of processes involved in designing, developing, deploying, and managing AI systems, where responsibilities must be clearly defined.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Value Chain refers to the series of processes and entities involved in the development, implementation, and regulation of artificial intelligence technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain represents the various stages of developing and deploying artificial intelligence systems, emphasizing responsibilities of different stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Value Chain encompasses all parties and processes involved in the development and deployment of AI systems, tools, and services.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain encompasses the various stages and processes involved in the development and deployment of artificial intelligence systems, highlighting the interconnections between different stakeholders such as providers and users of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management System">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A risk-management system for AI should be a continuous and iterative process aimed at identifying and mitigating risks associated with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A risk-management system is a structured approach to identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Requirements are the mandatory standards and regulations that products, especially those related to high-risk AI systems, must meet to be legally available in the Union market.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance requirements are the established standards and guidelines that AI systems must adhere to in order to ensure safety, reliability, and accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance requirements are the standards and guidelines that must be followed to ensure that high-risk AI systems and medical devices function safely and effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance requirements are the standards and guidelines that AI systems must meet to ensure safety and effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936246</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lifetime of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Lifetime of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The lifetime of AI systems encompasses all phases from development to retirement, during which performance, compliance, and safety must be continuously monitored.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934226</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Events and Logs">
      <data key="d0">Events and Logs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Events and logs refer to the automatic recording mechanisms that track the operations and performance of AI systems throughout their operational lifetime.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934226</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Level">
      <data key="d0">Union Level</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Level is a reference to the broader regulatory environment across member states where systemic risks associated with AI models must be addressed.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Level refers to the legislative and regulatory framework governing AI systems, specifically in the context of market surveillance and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Union level refers to the collective governance structure at which the regulations and codes of practice are enforced.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Level refers to the collective level of governance or decision-making within the Union related to transparency and AI content detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Level refers to the centralized governance and decision-making structure within the European Union regarding the regulation and implementation of AI policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_161.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_135.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936007</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commitments">
      <data key="d0">Commitments</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Commitments refer to binding agreements that providers of general-purpose AI models may offer to address identified systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of high-risk AI systems are entities tasked with the critical responsibility of ensuring that their AI technologies comply with applicable regulations and safety standards. These organizations must adhere to relevant regulations concerning the operation and management of AI systems, particularly those characterized by significant potential risks to users and society. They are responsible for designing and developing AI technologies that are classified as high-risk, akin to the operations of financial institutions and other regulated entities. Additionally, providers must demonstrate conformity with established requirements when requested by competent authorities, ensuring accountability and compliance in their deployment of AI systems in the market. Timely adherence to deadlines for regulatory compliance is also a key duty of these providers, highlighting their role in maintaining both safety and legal standards in the field of artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems refers to organizations or individuals that develop or deploy artificial intelligence technologies that pose significant risks and require specialized contractual terms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936290</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Declaration of Conformity">
      <data key="d0">EU Declaration of Conformity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Declaration of Conformity is a crucial legal document that certifies a product's compliance with European Union (EU) legislation and standards. It serves as a formal declaration made by the manufacturer, indicating that the product meets the necessary safety and performance requirements stipulated by EU regulations. This document is especially important for high-risk AI systems, which are required to provide the EU Declaration of Conformity as proof of compliance with specific regulations. By ensuring that products align with EU standards, the Declaration plays a vital role in maintaining safety and regulatory adherence within the European market.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Declaration of Conformity is a document affirming that a product meets the necessary regulatory standards and requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Declaration of Conformity is a document issued that certifies that a product meets the required standards, including cybersecurity requirements for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Declaration of Conformity is a document that confirms a product's compliance with EU regulations and directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management System">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Quality Management System is a structured system of processes and procedures required to ensure that high-risk AI systems comply with relevant regulations and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A quality management system is a structured system of procedures and responsibilities necessary for the management of quality within an organization.&lt;SEP&gt;A quality management system is a structured framework aimed at ensuring consistent quality in products and services, particularly in high-risk sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935868</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accessibility Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Accessibility Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessibility requirements are standards set forth to ensure products and services are accessible to individuals with disabilities, in accordance with the EU directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 17">
      <data key="d0">Article 17</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 17 is a section of the Regulation that discusses the quality management system requirements for microenterprises.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 17 outlines the necessity for a quality management system to be implemented by providers of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 17 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 is a legislative section that discusses the implementation of acts related to Artificial Intelligence systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e4f07f79ad3c90c82b86c0a02d0fae9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa</data>
