      <data key="d5">1783935589</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 19">
      <data key="d0">Article 19</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 19 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 establishes guidelines concerning delegated acts for Artificial Intelligence systems and their safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 outlines the provisions regarding the actions that market surveillance authorities must take when addressing high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 19 requires that logs automatically generated by high-risk AI systems be maintained for monitoring purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935589</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 43">
      <data key="d0">Article 43</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 43 details the procedures for conformity assessment that must be followed for CE marking compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 outlines the conformity assessment procedures that notified bodies must follow for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 refers to the conformity assessment procedure that high-risk AI systems must undergo prior to market release.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 pertains to the adoption of implementing acts for Artificial Intelligence systems focusing on safety components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a</data>
