    <node id="United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities">
      <data key="d0">United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities is an international human rights treaty aimed at protecting the rights and dignity of persons with disabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934237</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/2102">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/2102</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/2102 is a legal framework established for ensuring the accessibility of websites and mobile applications of public sector bodies in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2019/882">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2019/882</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2019/882 is a legislative measure enacted by the European Parliament and Council that establishes harmonized rules for the accessibility of products and services within the European Union. It aims to ensure compliance with its requirements by making products available on the market and regulating the accessibility, availability, and usability of information related to these products in the EU database.

The directive is particularly focused on ensuring that products and services are accessible to persons with disabilities, thereby promoting inclusivity and equal opportunities. It also outlines specific accessibility requirements that affect consumer rights and protections, demonstrating a commitment to creating a safe and equitable environment for all users. 

Furthermore, Directive (EU) 2019/882 aims to provide a high level of protection against harmful artificial intelligence systems and regulates AI practices to prevent the distortion of human behavior, especially for vulnerable groups. Overall, the directive underscores the EU's dedication to safeguarding rights and ensuring that all consumers, regardless of their abilities, can access and benefit from available products and services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17045c951f494f621b2305960aade53f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Technologies">
      <data key="d0">AI Technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Technologies refer to various advanced technologies involving artificial intelligence, including data computing and automation systems, which are regulated by competent authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Technologies refers to systems and tools based on artificial intelligence that require compliance with accessibility standards to serve all users effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;AI technologies refer to advanced systems that utilize artificial intelligence, categorized as high-risk based on their potential impact.&lt;SEP&gt;AI technologies encompass advancements in artificial intelligence which are crucial for the competence and functioning of the national authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Persons with Disabilities">
      <data key="d0">Persons with Disabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Persons with Disabilities refers to individuals who have long-term physical, mental, intellectual, or sensory impairments that may hinder their full and effective participation in society on an equal basis with others.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons with Disabilities represent a demographic that could benefit from AI solutions designed to enhance accessibility and inclusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons with disabilities are individuals with physical or mental impairments that may limit their full participation in society and require specific attention and accessibility measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c7912c5a4fb8a11a998bec401999088b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_142.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934909</data>
    </node>
