      <data key="d5">1783934579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Fraud">
      <data key="d0">Financial Fraud</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial fraud refers to deception intended to secure an unfair or unlawful financial gain, often targeted by AI risk analytics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4274f38f6b4aeff6dc2959e9e1a87f1a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_42.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934272</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Narcotics Trafficking">
      <data key="d0">Narcotics Trafficking</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Narcotics trafficking involves the illegal trade of illegal drugs, which may be addressed through predictive analytics in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4274f38f6b4aeff6dc2959e9e1a87f1a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_42.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934272</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Authority">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Judicial Authority is an independent body that grants prior authorization for the use of remote biometric identification systems in law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authorities are institutions responsible for administering justice, interpreting laws, and ensuring a fair trial within the legal system.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial Authorities are responsible for making binding decisions on legal matters, including the authorisation for using high-risk AI systems in criminal investigations.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial Authority refers to the court or governing body that oversees legal compliance and authorization for the use of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Alternative Dispute Resolution Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Alternative Dispute Resolution Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Alternative dispute resolution bodies facilitate the resolution of disputes outside the court system, often yielding legally binding outcomes for the involved parties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Justice Administration">
      <data key="d0">Justice Administration</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Justice administration pertains to the processes and practices involved in the enforcement of laws and the adjudication of legal disputes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human-Driven Decision Making">
      <data key="d0">Human-Driven Decision Making</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human-driven decision making emphasizes that final legal decisions should be made by humans, enhancing judicial independence and preventing overreliance on AI tools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Democratic Processes">
      <data key="d0">Democratic Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Democratic Processes include the systems and practices that allow a society to function as a democracy, including elections and public participation.&lt;SEP&gt;Democratic processes refer to the systems and methods used to ensure fair governance, including the administration of justice and legal proceedings.&lt;SEP&gt;Democratic processes involve the mechanisms of governance that allow citizens to participate in decision-making, which can be threatened by disinformation or bias from AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f46abe104a1bdb0fae1c25094db36d</data>
