      <data key="d5">1783935457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Decision-Making">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Decision-Making</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial decision-making is the process carried out by judges to interpret laws and apply them to specific cases, ensuring fair and just outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biases in AI">
      <data key="d0">Biases in AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biases in AI refer to the potential prejudices that may arise during the operation of AI systems, affecting their decision-making and outcomes in judicial contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency in AI">
      <data key="d0">Transparency in AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency in AI refers to the clarity with which AI processes operate, ensuring their decisions can be understood and scrutinized to uphold fairness and justice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Rights">
      <data key="d0">Human Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human rights are the fundamental guarantees provided to individuals, which include the right to fair trial and effective remedy in judicial proceedings.&lt;SEP&gt;Human rights are the inalienable fundamental rights entitled to every human being, often at risk due to the misuse of technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392a0705db576351b9cbccd6dcfdf33f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_110.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter V">
      <data key="d0">Chapter V</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter V is a section within the regulation that details obligations related to harmonised standards for various sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter V refers to a section of legislative text that outlines specific regulations and obligations related to AI systems within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter V refers to a specific section within a regulation that is under the scrutiny and enforcement of The Commission, likely detailing certain legal or procedural standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter V of the Regulation specifies additional rules coming into force at a later date, affecting compliance and legal responsibilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656</data>
