      <data key="d0">Border Control Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Border control management encompasses activities and strategies implemented by authorities to monitor and control the entry and exit of individuals across national borders.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control management encompasses the policies and practices used to regulate access to a country, often involving high-risk AI systems for monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control management encompasses the policies and practices employed by states to regulate the entry and exit of individuals across borders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administration of Justice">
      <data key="d0">Administration of Justice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administration of Justice entails the legal systems through which public services are rendered, potentially impacted by AI technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Administration of justice refers to the process and institutions involved in ensuring fair application of laws and the provision of justice in legal matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934928</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Data Protection Directive 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">EU Data Protection Directive 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/680 outlines the data protection standards specific to law enforcement and ensures personal data rights are upheld during processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 31">
      <data key="d0">Article 31</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 31 outlines a set of specific requirements and standards that conformity assessment bodies must meet to be eligible for notification. It details the obligations that both these bodies and their subcontractors or subsidiaries must satisfy. Additionally, Article 31 provides procedural guidelines for the notification and assessment of organizations responsible for overseeing compliance with high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Overall, Article 31 serves as a crucial provision within a regulatory framework, ensuring that conformity assessment bodies adhere to harmonised standards to maintain high compliance and safety levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 refers to a specific provision in regulatory texts that outlines the requirements for conformity assessment bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 outlines essential requirements for notified bodies regarding their obligations and the consequences of failing to meet these requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 outlines the requirements and responsibilities of notified bodies as part of regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b479c56b927c79a74d3a19d8470ff1da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 29">
      <data key="d0">Article 29</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 29 outlines the procedures related to the extensions and changes of the notifications provided by notified bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 29 specifies the accreditation and documentation requirements necessary for compliance assessment notifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935839</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notifying Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Notifying Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Notifying Authorities are designated entities responsible for the conformity assessment process, ensuring objectivity and impartiality.&lt;SEP&gt;Notifying Authorities are involved in market surveillance and are invited to Board discussions about related compliance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Notifying Authorities are responsible for notifying market surveillance authorities about relevant issues and compliance matters.&lt;SEP&gt;Notifying authorities are designated bodies within Member States that are responsible for communicating information to the Commission regarding regulatory compliance and market surveillance.&lt;SEP&gt;Notifying authorities are responsible for notifying conformity assessment bodies and ensuring compliance with laid-out requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accreditation Certificate">
      <data key="d0">Accreditation Certificate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An Accreditation Certificate is a formal document that proves a conformity assessment body meets the necessary requirements set by an accrediting authority.&lt;SEP&gt;An accreditation certificate serves as official documentation indicating that a conformity assessment body meets established competency requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935510</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentary Evidence">
      <data key="d0">Documentary Evidence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentary Evidence includes all necessary documentation that a conformity assessment body must provide to support its compliance with the requirements of regulatory bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentary evidence refers to the paperwork submitted to prove a conformity assessment body's competence in operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935510</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Two Weeks">
      <data key="d0">Two Weeks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Two weeks is the timeframe within which objections to notifications must be raised to conforming assessment bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Two Months">
      <data key="d0">Two Months</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Two months is the period allowed for objections to be raised when documentary evidence is involved in the notification process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex I">
      <data key="d0">Annex I</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex I is a segment of the legal framework that encompasses Union harmonization legislation pertinent to high-risk AI systems. This section outlines a comprehensive monitoring system and plan designed to ensure compliance with regulatory standards and to protect the safety of AI systems in the market. It specifies the safety standards that products must meet to align with Union legislation, and includes detailed provisions for post-market monitoring and market surveillance. Overall, Annex I serves as a crucial element in the regulation of product safety and compliance standards within the European Union, specifically targeting high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I lists legal acts that govern the conformity assessment process for AI systems, including provisions for third-party assessments and harmonised standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I outlines the specific AI systems that have a maximum certificate validity period of five years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936246</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Financial Services Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Financial Services Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Financial Services Law refers to a comprehensive framework of regulations that govern the operation and internal arrangements of financial institutions within the European Union. This body of law encompasses various aspects including governance and quality management criteria, specifically addressing the internal governance processes and compliance practices related to the deployment of artificial intelligence (AI) systems by these institutions. It is designed to impact the internal governance and regulatory compliance of financial entities, ensuring that they adhere to established standards while effectively integrating advanced technologies in their operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Union financial services law refers to regulatory standards governing financial institutions and their operations, particularly concerning internal processes and documentation requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union financial services law">
      <data key="d0">Union financial services law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union financial services law pertains to regulations governing financial institutions and their internal processes in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Financial Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Institutions are entities that provide a range of financial services, which include banks and investment firms, and are regulated under the Union financial services law. This legal framework imposes specific governance and compliance requirements to ensure that these organizations adhere to established standards. Additionally, Financial Institutions must implement internal governance and quality management systems as dictated by Union financial services law. Furthermore, these organizations may also deploy high-risk AI systems, which necessitates additional internal governance measures to mitigate potential risks. Overall, Financial Institutions play a crucial role in the financial sector while being bound by strict regulatory oversight to maintain financial stability and consumer protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial Institutions are entities that provide financial services, such as banks and investment firms, and are subject to EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial institutions are organizations that provide financial services and are subject to regulations relevant to their internal governance practices, particularly in the context of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legislation">
      <data key="d0">Legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legislation encompasses laws and regulations established to govern the use and market of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Legislation refers to laws and regulations enacted to manage various sectors, including technology and AI, ensuring safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935777</data>
    </node>
    <node id="deep fakes">
      <data key="d0">deep fakes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep fakes are synthetic media in which a person in an existing image or video is replaced with someone else's likeness, often raising concerns about authenticity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI system providers">
      <data key="d0">AI system providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">AI system providers are entities that create and manage AI technologies designed to generate or manipulate multimedia content, including images, audio, and video.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="deployers">
      <data key="d0">deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are organizations or individuals that utilize AI systems to produce or alter content, such as deep fakes, ensuring compliance with transparency regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers have specific requirements and obligations as per Article 26, relating to the deployment of products and services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="transparency obligation">
      <data key="d0">transparency obligation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The transparency obligation refers to the requirement that users of AI systems disclose the artificial origin of generated or manipulated content to the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="artistic works">
      <data key="d0">artistic works</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Artistic works encompass creative outputs, including artistic, satirical, and fictional content, that may utilize AI technologies while raising ethical considerations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="public interest">
      <data key="d0">public interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public interest refers to matters that affect the community at large and warrant responsible dissemination of content, especially when involving AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interest refers to the welfare or well-being of the general public, guiding the justification for certain law enforcement actions and measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934474</data>
    </node>
    <node id="human review or editorial control">
      <data key="d0">human review or editorial control</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human review or editorial control indicates processes that can exempt AI-generated content from disclosure requirements if applied prior to publication.&lt;SEP&gt;Human review or editorial control involves the oversight of AI-generated content by individuals to ensure accuracy, clarity, and compliance with ethical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-generated content">
      <data key="d0">AI-generated content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-generated content refers to material produced by artificial intelligence algorithms, often requiring human oversight for quality and reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="natural or legal person">
      <data key="d0">natural or legal person</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural or legal person is an individual or legal entity that can hold rights and obligations, particularly in relation to editorial responsibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-Generated Content">
      <data key="d0">AI-Generated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-Generated Content refers to content produced by artificial intelligence without human intervention, often necessitating editorial oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Review">
      <data key="d0">Human Review</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Review relates to the process where human oversight is applied to AI-generated content to ensure compliance with established ethical guidelines and accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Human Review signifies the process where content is evaluated by a person to ensure accuracy, quality, and adherence to standards before publication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Editorial Control">
      <data key="d0">Editorial Control</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Editorial Control involves managing the content publication process to ensure it meets specific quality and ethical standards, often involving checks for misinformation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Interest">
      <data key="d0">Public Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Interest denotes matters that are relevant to the community and society, particularly regarding the use of AI and its ethical considerations in content generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Interest represents the welfare or well-being of the general public, often guiding the need for accurate information dissemination in media.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
