    <node id="Self-Supervised Learning">
      <data key="d0">Self-Supervised Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-Supervised Learning is a method used to train AI models by allowing them to generate labels from the input data itself, enhancing their learning capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unsupervised Learning">
      <data key="d0">Unsupervised Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Unsupervised Learning is a technique in machine learning used to train models on data without explicit labels, focusing on finding hidden patterns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reinforcement Learning">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Reinforcement Learning is an approach in machine learning where an agent learns to make decisions by receiving rewards or penalties based on its actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Libraries">
      <data key="d0">Libraries</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Libraries are repositories that provide access to various General-Purpose AI Models, enabling developers to utilize pre-trained models for application development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934325</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Application Programming Interfaces (APIs)">
      <data key="d0">Application Programming Interfaces (APIs)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">APIs are sets of protocols that allow different software applications to communicate with each other, often used for integrating AI models into external software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_97.json</data>
