    <node id="Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations are legal or institutional requirements that entities must adhere to, particularly concerning compliance with various regulations associated with artificial intelligence (AI) models. These obligations encompass legal requirements imposed on providers of AI models, which dictate adherence to standards of copyright compliance in their operations. Furthermore, obligations involve responsibilities placed on organizations to ensure compliance with specific regulations, which include aspects related to quality management and governance. They also refer to the legal or ethical responsibilities that providers are required to fulfill regarding the use of AI systems. Additionally, obligations detail the specific requirements and responsibilities mandated by regulations for providers of AI systems and outline the necessary duties concerning the administration and operation of these systems within the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations refer to the regulatory requirements and responsibilities that notified bodies must fulfill to retain their designation status.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations refer to the regulatory responsibilities that providers of general-purpose AI models must adhere to, aimed at mitigating systemic risks and ensuring safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
