    </node>
    <node id="High-risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">High-risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI Systems are classified under specific legal acts identified by the Union harmonisation legislation that require enhanced scrutiny and monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are AI technologies that require specialized oversight to prevent risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to artificial intelligence technologies that carry significant risks and require compliance with specific regulations, including bearing the CE marking.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are categorized as those systems that require stringent testing and regulations, particularly in sensitive fields such as law enforcement and migration.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are artificial intelligence applications that must comply with specific regulatory requirements to ensure safety and reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935947</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Oversight">
      <data key="d0">Human Oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Oversight involves the human supervision required in the operation and monitoring of AI systems to ensure adherence to guidelines and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight refers to the intervention and monitoring by natural persons to manage and mitigate risks associated with the use of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight is a crucial component in the management of high-risk AI systems to ensure ethical considerations and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_91.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human-Machine Interface Tools">
      <data key="d0">Human-Machine Interface Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human-machine interface tools are designed to facilitate effective interaction between high-risk AI systems and natural persons overseeing their use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934336</data>
