    <node id="Internal Market">
      <data key="d0">Internal Market</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Internal Market is a fundamental aspect of the European Union that allows goods, services, capital, and people to move freely among Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Internal Market refers to the integrated economy of the European Union, allowing free movement of goods, services, capital, and people among member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal market refers to the regulatory environment that allows for the free movement of goods and services within the European Union, aiming to create a unified economic space.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae8bdbb57af24d78fe2313201571bea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58</data>
