    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2022/2065">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 establishes comprehensive obligations and requirements for providers of AI systems and models operating within the European Union. It focuses particularly on those offering intermediary services, ensuring they have measures in place for the detection and disclosure of outputs that are artificially generated or manipulated. The regulation emphasizes a technology-neutral approach, applying to various AI systems used as intermediary services. Furthermore, it governs the liability of these service providers, detailing the legal obligations they must adhere to. This regulation is closely linked to the Digital Services Act, which aims to create a safer digital environment in the EU while addressing the responsibilities of intermediary service providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 outlines obligations for providers of certain AI systems to ensure transparency in outputs that are artificially generated or manipulated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ab686ea2085e0bf2cc7ea2cb5eb270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74def3a33d9c60f3c11227adf7704a09</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_119.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_136.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935668</data>
    </node>
