      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746 pertain to the safety and performance of medical devices, relevant for AI systems classified as safety components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Incidents">
      <data key="d0">Serious Incidents</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious incidents refer to significant failures or malfunctions that occur in high-risk AI systems, which must be reported to authorities per the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934453</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reporting Deployer">
      <data key="d0">Reporting Deployer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The reporting deployer is an entity that operates or uses the high-risk AI system and is involved in reporting risks and compliance issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934461</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributors">
      <data key="d0">Distributors</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Distributors are entities responsible for distributing AI systems within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are entities that handle the logistics of distributing high-risk AI systems to the market, and they need to be informed of compliance status.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are operators that supply AI systems to consumers and must comply with legal obligations associated with their role in the value chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are responsible for the distribution of products and must comply with relevant regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934801</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance is the process by which regulatory bodies monitor and ensure compliance of products, including technologies, with safety and performance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance is the system of monitoring and regulating high-risk AI systems to ensure they meet safety and compliance standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 79(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 79(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 79(1) outlines conditions under which high-risk AI systems may present a risk, necessitating careful monitoring and logging practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) outlines specific obligations for providers regarding risk management in high-risk AI systems, mandating timely action upon risk identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) pertains to the legal framework governing the compliance and regulatory obligations associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
