      <data key="d5">1783935952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 44">
      <data key="d0">Article 44</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 44 relates to the requirements for high-risk AI systems, particularly about conformity assessments made by notified bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934461</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Data Protection Regulation">
      <data key="d0">European Data Protection Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Regulation sets the legislative framework for data protection across the European Union, mandating how personal data should be handled by organizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Affected Persons">
      <data key="d0">Affected Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Affected persons are individuals located within the Union whose rights may be impacted by the use of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals whose rights may have been violated due to an infringement of data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals or groups who suffer harm or damages as a result of regulatory infringements and are considered when determining administrative fines.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals who may be significantly impacted by decisions made based on high-risk AI systems, particularly regarding their legal rights, health, safety, and fundamental freedoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_171.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Measures">
      <data key="d0">Technical Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Measures are actions or protocols that deployers must take to ensure the safe operation of AI systems, addressing potential risks associated with their deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical measures refer to the organizational controls and technological safeguards implemented by Union institutions to ensure compliance with data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical measures refer to the systems and methods implemented by operators to prevent legal infringements and mitigate their impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical measures refer to strategies and implementations aimed at ensuring the robustness and safe operation of high-risk AI systems to prevent undesirable outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f15de033aa4361b6dbf4b5d72ede05a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Organizational Measures">
      <data key="d0">Organizational Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Organizational measures involve policies and practices put in place to manage compliance with data protection regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Organizational measures pertain to the frameworks and guidelines set within organizations to manage risks associated with high-risk AI systems, aimed at enhancing safety and operational integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f15de033aa4361b6dbf4b5d72ede05a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Data Protection Supervisor's Opportunity to Be Heard">
      <data key="d0">European Data Protection Supervisor's Opportunity to Be Heard</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Supervisor's Opportunity to Be Heard is a procedural right allowing Union institutions to defend themselves against claims of infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union institution, body, office or agency">
      <data key="d0">Union institution, body, office or agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A generic term referring to any official entity within the European Union, including various institutions, bodies, offices, and agencies involved in governance and regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Practices referred to in Article 5">
      <data key="d0">AI Practices referred to in Article 5</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI practices mentioned in Article 5 represent specific prohibitive actions that the European Data Protection Supervisor monitors to ensure compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Supervisor">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Supervisor</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Data Protection Supervisor is an organization responsible for overseeing the protection of personal data and business secrets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Litigation or Judicial Proceedings">
      <data key="d0">Litigation or Judicial Proceedings</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Litigation or Judicial Proceedings refer to the legal actions initiated by the European Data Protection Supervisor as part of its enforcement activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fines">
      <data key="d0">Fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fines are monetary penalties imposed as a consequence of certain actions or violations, which must be effective, proportionate, and dissuasive according to the Article.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines are monetary penalties imposed for non-compliance with regulations, including those related to AI model provisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines refer to monetary penalties imposed on individuals or organizations for non-compliance with data protection regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935920</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legitimate Interest">
      <data key="d0">Legitimate Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legitimate Interest is a legal basis under data protection laws that allows for the processing of personal data when it serves a legitimate purpose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General Budget of the Union">
      <data key="d0">General Budget of the Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The General Budget of the Union is the financial framework within which funds, including those from imposed fines, are managed and allocated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Competent Authority">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Competent Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A relevant competent authority is a regulatory body that oversees the compliance and safety of high-risk AI systems, intervening to enforce regulations if necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;Relevant Competent Authorities are regulatory bodies that supervise and enforce compliance of high-risk AI systems to ensure safety and conformity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 16 &amp; 23 Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Article 16 &amp; 23 Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 16 and 23 outline the obligations and responsibilities of providers and importers for high-risk AI systems under European regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 23(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 23(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 23(3) sets forth additional compliance obligations for entities involved with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934471</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Authority">
      <data key="d0">Competent Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A competent authority is an entity that has the power to request information from providers of high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A competent authority is an organization responsible for overseeing compliance with regulations, particularly in relation to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent Authorities are designated bodies responsible for enforcing compliance and safety regulations concerning high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing compliance and safety standards for high-risk AI systems and addressing non-compliance issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935670</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real-time remote biometric identification systems">
      <data key="d0">real-time remote biometric identification systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-time remote biometric identification systems are advanced technologies used in law enforcement to identify individuals based on biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technological solutions used in public spaces to identify individuals through biometric data for law enforcement purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technologies used for identifying individuals in publicly accessible spaces, primarily for law enforcement purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="criminal offences">
      <data key="d0">criminal offences</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal offences refer to legally defined acts that are punishable by law, with a focus on serious crimes as defined in the annex to Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934474</data>
    </node>
    <node id="missing persons">
      <data key="d0">missing persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Missing persons are individuals whose whereabouts are unknown, often prompting law enforcement searches based on public interest and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934474</data>
    </node>
    <node id="victims of crime">
      <data key="d0">victims of crime</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Victims of crime are individuals who have suffered harm due to criminal acts, such as theft, assault, or other offenses, and may require law enforcement assistance for recovery and justice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934474</data>
    </node>
    <node id="terrorist attack">
      <data key="d0">terrorist attack</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A terrorist attack involves unlawful acts intended to intimidate or coerce a population or government, prompting law enforcement responses to threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934474</data>
    </node>
    <node id="custodial sentence">
      <data key="d0">custodial sentence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A custodial sentence is a court-ordered penalty involving confinement in a prison or similar facility due to serious criminal offenses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934474</data>
    </node>
    <node id="detention order">
      <data key="d0">detention order</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A detention order is a legal authorization to hold a person in custody, usually related to law enforcement actions following serious crimes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
