      <data key="d5">1783934478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Crime">
      <data key="d0">Crime</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Crime refers to actions that are violations of laws and can involve individuals who may hide their identity from authorities for various reasons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6badc71855b10bbd17a31c7dfef0c442</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Arrest Warrant">
      <data key="d0">European Arrest Warrant</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Arrest Warrant is a legal framework that enables the extradition of criminal suspects between EU Member States, part of the Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6badc71855b10bbd17a31c7dfef0c442</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competence and Resource Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Competence and Resource Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Competence and resource requirements pertain to the necessary qualifications, skills, and infrastructures needed for national competent authorities to perform their tasks effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934497</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electronic Communication Means">
      <data key="d0">Electronic Communication Means</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electronic communication means are the methods by which Member States must publicly share the contact information of competent authorities and single points of contact.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934497</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national competent authorities">
      <data key="d0">national competent authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National competent authorities are designated bodies within Member States responsible for ensuring the compliance of AI systems with established standards.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are designated governmental bodies within individual EU member states that are responsible for overseeing the implementation and enforcement of regulations related to artificial intelligence (AI) technologies. Their primary role involves ensuring compliance with established standards in cybersecurity and personal data protection, especially concerning high-risk AI systems. Additionally, these authorities are tasked with enforcing compliance with EU regulations and may issue penalties for regulatory infringements. In summary, national competent authorities play a crucial role in maintaining regulatory standards and ensuring that AI models comply with Union law across the member states.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are responsible for enforcing regulations and notifying bodies under the specified Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-595952fa3e7e47cb312adaaad303b73c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935839</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety Risks">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and Safety Risks refer to potential dangers that can arise from the use of AI technologies and requires evaluation by competent authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety risks pertain to potential dangers and negative outcomes that can arise from the deployment of high-risk AI systems, necessitating thorough risk assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member States Reporting">
      <data key="d0">Member States Reporting</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States Reporting is the process where EU member states evaluate and report on their national competent authorities' resources and adequacy regarding AI regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934502</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2005 Regulation">
      <data key="d0">2005 Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The 2005 Regulation refers to the legislative framework established for the oversight of AI technologies and their impact on personal data protection and cybersecurity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934502</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union institutions">
      <data key="d0">Union institutions</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2ba08954f9ed754c2566e3c59b63ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the competent authority overseeing Union institutions and bodies under the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions refer to the entities and organizations established within the framework of the Union, responsible for various functions including the deployment of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934606</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-on-demand platform">
      <data key="d0">AI-on-demand platform</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI-on-demand platform is an initiative aimed at supporting the implementation of AI technologies through technical and scientific assistance to providers.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI-on-demand platform is an organization focused on promoting and protecting innovation within the framework of Union funding programmes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86aff1d72a3f6226d0b5db29d9910a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_145.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_144.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Digital Innovation Hubs">
      <data key="d0">European Digital Innovation Hubs</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">European Digital Innovation Hubs are centers designed to aid businesses, primarily SMEs and start-ups, in leveraging digital technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs are institutions aimed at supporting businesses in digital transformation and compliance with regulatory standards in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs provide support and resources for innovation in digital technologies, including AI, to foster growth and compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs are entities designed to support the digital transformation of businesses and public sectors by facilitating access to digital technologies, training, and data resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_145.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936291</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs)">
      <data key="d0">Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">SMEs are businesses whose interests and needs are taken into account when developing AI governance frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) refer to smaller businesses that face specific challenges in complying with regulations and accessing expertise in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;SMEs include small and medium-sized businesses that benefit from reduced barriers to access markets through AI regulatory sandboxes, fostering innovation and development in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) are businesses that are targeted by the regulation to support innovation in the AI sector.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5928be36056ac91865bd3e4d596159e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_145.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_1.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936327</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU declaration of conformity">
      <data key="d0">EU declaration of conformity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU declaration of conformity is a formal document that certifies high-risk AI systems comply with established legal requirements and must be maintained for 10 years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_47.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex V">
      <data key="d0">Annex V</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex V is an attachment to regulations that contains specific information regarding compliance requirements and the EU declaration of conformity.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex V outlines specific requirements for the EU declaration of conformity, detailing necessary compliance information for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_47.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Governance and Management Practices">
      <data key="d0">Data Governance and Management Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data governance and management practices are essential for ensuring the quality and appropriateness of data sets used in high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Data governance and management practices comprise strategies and protocols for managing data assets to ensure quality, compliance, and protection against bias and errors in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934740</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Training Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training data sets are collections of data used to train AI models, ensuring they can make accurate predictions or decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data sets are crucial for AI model development, but they can be susceptible to data poisoning attacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5765a06abb615496a937c9303e1583cd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Validation Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Validation data sets are used to tune model parameters and assess the performance of AI systems during development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934513</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Testing Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing data sets evaluate the final model's effectiveness before deployment, ensuring its reliability and accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934513</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Quality Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Data Quality Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data quality criteria are standards set to ensure that the data used in AI systems is accurate, complete, and free of bias.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934513</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bias Detection Measures">
      <data key="d0">Bias Detection Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias detection measures are practices applied to identify and mitigate biases that may affect AI system outputs and subsequent decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934513</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Geographical Context">
      <data key="d0">Geographical Context</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Geographical context entails the specific location-related factors that need to be considered in AI data sets.&lt;SEP&gt;Geographical context relates to the specific location characteristics that must be taken into account when designing high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
