    <node id="Biometric Categorisation Systems">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Categorisation Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric Categorisation Systems categorize individuals based on their biometric data, potentially inferring sensitive personal attributes.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric categorisation systems are tools used to classify individuals based on biometric data, such as facial recognition and fingerprints, for various purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric categorisation systems refer to systems that use biometric data, like facial recognition and fingerprints, to infer personal information about individuals, such as political opinions and beliefs.</data>
