    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2016/680 addresses the processing of personal data by competent authorities for law enforcement purposes, ensuring fundamental rights and privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/680 establishes provisions regarding data protection and establishes market surveillance activities among other regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/680 pertains to the protection of individuals with regard to the processing of personal data by competent authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/680 is a directive that focuses on the protection of personal data processed for law enforcement purposes, ensuring compliance with privacy standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI systems">
      <data key="d0">AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems encompass a wide range of technologies that utilize artificial intelligence for various applications, including data processing, translation, and profiling. These systems are characterized by their categorization according to risk levels as outlined in regulatory frameworks. Non-high-risk systems are specified in regulations, while high-risk systems are accompanied by defined use cases. AI systems operate based on algorithms and models that analyze data inputs, impacting future operations and outcomes. They are designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence and must comply with regulatory standards. Additionally, AI systems are employed in specific areas such as migration, asylum, and border control management, where they assist public authorities in evaluating and managing border-related processes. Overall, AI systems represent a significant and regulated sector of technology that plays a crucial role in various fields and applications.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems refer to artificial intelligence technologies that perform tasks requiring human intelligence, including those related to decision-making and content generation.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems refer to various technologies and algorithms used to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, posing potential risks and requiring mandatory regulations for high-risk categories.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c168b1207668ad4ba646371f91bfce09</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_124.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935773</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU database">
      <data key="d0">EU database</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU database is a centralized repository managed by the European Commission, specifically designed for the registration of high-risk AI systems across various sectors, including law enforcement and critical infrastructure. This database aims to ensure both registration and traceability of these high-risk systems, facilitating effective oversight and compliance with relevant regulations. Mandated by Union regulations, the EU database not only registers these AI systems but also promotes transparency and accessibility to the public concerning their operation.

The structured nature of the EU database allows for the storage of essential information related to compliance with legal standards, encompassing aspects such as testing and regulatory oversight of AI systems. By collecting and processing relevant data, the EU database plays a crucial role in ensuring that high-risk AI systems adhere to necessary regulations and contribute to informed public awareness regarding their usage and the potential risks involved. Overall, the EU database serves as a vital tool in enhancing market oversight and maintaining rigorous standards for high-risk AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU database refers to a secure non-public section where data related to high-risk AI systems testing is stored and managed in accordance with Union law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935794</data>
    </node>
