    <node id="Article 73">
      <data key="d0">Article 73</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 73 governs the procedures related to the reporting of serious incidents involving high-risk AI systems, mandating communication with relevant authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 73 sets forth procedures for reporting serious incidents involving high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 73 pertains to specific legal provisions outlined in EU regulations that guide compliance for the deployment of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 73 requires the reporting of serious incidents identified during the testing of AI systems, establishing a framework for accountability and safety measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 73 pertains to serious incident reports as part of regulatory evaluations within the EU framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0</data>
