      <data key="d5">1783934685</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Central Bank">
      <data key="d0">European Central Bank</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Central Bank (ECB) is a pivotal institution that serves as the central bank for the euro and is primarily responsible for administering monetary policy within the Eurozone. Its core functions include overseeing the monetary policy of the Eurozone and ensuring financial stability by supervising banking practices and credit institutions. Additionally, the ECB coordinates its efforts with national authorities to effectively manage and implement these policies. Through its responsibilities, the ECB plays a crucial role in maintaining economic stability within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfa4c0995d224333f53196e26a30156b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2013/36/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2013/36/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2013/36/EU is a comprehensive European regulation that governs access to the activities of credit institutions and establishes a framework for their prudential supervision within the European Union. This directive outlines essential regulations concerning the governance and risk management of credit institutions, aiming to ensure financial stability within the EU. It pertains not only to credit institutions but also extends to the activities of investment firms, emphasizing the importance of effective supervision. By setting forth requirements for these entities, Directive 2013/36/EU plays a vital role in underpinning the integrity of EU financial frameworks and promoting sound risk management practices among credit institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934979</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single Supervisory Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Single Supervisory Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Single Supervisory Mechanism is a system established to ensure effective supervision of credit institutions in the Eurozone under the European Central Bank's oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Single Supervisory Mechanism is a system of banking supervision in the Eurozone, designed to ensure the safety and soundness of credit institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Single Supervisory Mechanism is a system for banking supervision in the Eurozone, ensuring consistent supervision across participating countries.&lt;SEP&gt;The Single Supervisory Mechanism is a system of banking supervision for the Eurozone, established to ensure the safety and soundness of financial institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems (Annex III)">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems (Annex III)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI Systems listed in Annex III are defined as AI technologies that require stringent regulatory oversight due to their significant impact on safety or fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934690</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 establishes the Single Supervisory Mechanism for banking oversight within the Eurozone.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 establishes the framework for the Single Supervisory Mechanism in the EU, focusing on banking supervision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/679 is a regulation in EU law on data protection and privacy that establishes protocols for processing personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2016/679, also known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), is a comprehensive data protection law in the EU that sets guidelines for the collection and processing of personal information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Court of Justice of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Court of Justice of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Court of Justice of the European Union is the highest court in the European Union, responsible for ensuring EU law is interpreted and applied uniformly across member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice operates in its judicial capacity and is not subject to oversight by market surveillance authorities under the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union is the judicial authority that reviews decisions made by the Commission regarding fines and other regulatory measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union is the judicial institution responsible for ensuring compliance with EU law and has jurisdiction to review decisions made by the European Commission regarding fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935914</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 41 to 44">
      <data key="d0">Articles 41 to 44</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 41 to 44 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 outline conditions related to market surveillance activities for designated authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="API">
      <data key="d0">API</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">API, or application programming interfaces, are technical means provided for accessing data used in the training and development of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Application programming interfaces (API) allow for technical means enabling remote access to data sets and documentation related to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality obligations refer to the legal requirements to protect information obtained by market surveillance authorities under Article 78.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authorities' Access">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authorities' Access</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance authorities' access refers to the permissions granted to authorities to obtain documentation and data sets for auditing high-risk AI systems under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Source Code Access">
      <data key="d0">Source Code Access</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Source code access is the ability of market surveillance authorities to examine the underlying code of high-risk AI systems when certain conditions are met.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System Data">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI system data includes the training, validation, and testing data sets essential for the development and auditing of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter III, Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Chapter III, Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter III, Section 2 encompasses provisions from both Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 regarding artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This section delineates the specific requirements that high-risk AI systems must fulfill to achieve compliance, emphasizing ethical application and governance. Moreover, it addresses the requirements and standards for safety components of artificial intelligence systems, providing comprehensive guidelines concerning their use and approval. By combining these elements, Chapter III, Section 2 serves as a critical framework ensuring that AI systems not only meet safety and compliance standards but also adhere to ethical considerations in their deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935663</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data and Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Data and Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data and documentation refers to the materials provided by AI system providers that market surveillance authorities inspect to ensure compliance with the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Institutions">
      <data key="d0">EU Institutions</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the market surveillance authority for EU institutions, ensuring their compliance with data protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934695</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Organisations">
      <data key="d0">International Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">International Organisations are entities established by treaties between multiple countries to engage in activities of mutual interest, often supporting law enforcement and judicial cooperation.&lt;SEP&gt;International Organisations are entities established by treaty and composed of member states, often engaged in cooperative frameworks with the EU on various issues.&lt;SEP&gt;International organisations are entities involved in global cooperation that may implement AI systems under specific regulations in conjunction with the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;International organisations work on AI to facilitate global standards, convergence, and acceptance of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;International Organisations are entities that collaborate with Union institutions and Member States to promote global cooperation on standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd27f4cf61449e217b2273c0cf67adfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorized Representatives">
      <data key="d0">Authorized Representatives</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorized representatives act on behalf of providers not established in the Union, ensuring compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934705</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Military AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Military AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Military AI systems are those designed for use in defense or national security contexts, and are exempt from certain regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934705</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 24">
      <data key="d0">Recital 24</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 24 refers to a specific section of the Regulation that outlines the non-application of the law to certain military or national security-related AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934705</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 22">
      <data key="d0">Recital 22</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 22 pertains to the clauses defining the relationship between international organizations and the Union regarding the use of AI systems under specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934705</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2002/58/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2002/58/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2002/58/EC addresses privacy and electronic communications, relevant to the protection of data in connection with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC focuses on the privacy and electronic communications within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC aims to safeguard private life and confidentiality in electronic communications, including data storage and access from terminal equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC pertains to personal data processing and privacy in electronic communications.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC pertains to the processing of personal data and privacy in the electronic communications sector.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3cb5eb81289d4fb565bd824bdc63506&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935987</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter II">
      <data key="d0">Chapter II</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter II of the Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 outlines the liability of providers of intermediary services related to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter II of the Regulation complements the first chapter by providing further detailed regulations applying from a specified date.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Workers">
      <data key="d0">Workers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Workers are individuals employed who have rights to be informed and consulted about high-risk AI systems and other workplace issues arising under Union or national law.&lt;SEP&gt;Workers refer to individuals employed and engaged in professions that may be impacted by regulations concerning the use of AI systems in their workplace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c664ec81872dda212b64d449aa7a2014</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935897</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Protection Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Protection Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer Protection Regulations are legal provisions designed to ensure the safety and rights of consumers in relation to products and services, including AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency requirements dictate that high-risk AI systems must provide clear information about their operations, limitations, and intended uses to ensure informed decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Oversight Measures">
      <data key="d0">Human Oversight Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human oversight measures are protocols established to monitor high-risk AI systems' operations to ensure they adhere to safety and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight measures refer to protocols that ensure human involvement in the operation of high-risk AI systems to mitigate risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight measures involve technical implementations that ensure human operators can interpret high-risk AI system outputs and manage their use.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight measures entail specific protocols and actions designed to guide natural persons in their roles concerning AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936012</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Target Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Target Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Target deployers are the individuals or organizations intended to utilize the AI system, who must understand the instructions for correct usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A formal record provided by AI model providers detailing the capabilities and usage of their AI models, essential for regulatory compliance and transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentation includes all written materials and guidelines that accompany the AI system, ensuring users understand its proper use and limitations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2014/31/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2014/31/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2014/31/EU is a law that pertains to the harmonisation of standards for non-automatic weighing instruments within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934728</data>
