    <node id="Member States of the EU">
      <data key="d0">Member States of the EU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States of the EU refers to the individual countries that are part of the European Union, obliged to comply with EU directives and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4fa1ad79284c6e1a9636113352a8e0f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934738</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data sets are collections of related data used for training, validation, and testing AI systems, essential for ensuring their performance and compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Data sets refer to collections of data used for training or testing AI systems, which should be complete and free of errors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934740</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bias">
      <data key="d0">Bias</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias refers to systematic deviations in data that can lead to unfair outcomes in AI systems, particularly impacting certain individuals or groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Bias refers to the systematic favoritism or prejudice that can manifest in machine learning models, potentially leading to unfair treatment of individuals or groups.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392a0705db576351b9cbccd6dcfdf33f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_110.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Law">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection Law refers to legal principles that govern the processing of personal data, aimed at protecting individuals' privacy and data rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Data protection law encompasses legal frameworks that govern how personal data is collected, processed, and stored in order to protect individual privacy rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Data protection law refers to regulations that protect personal data and the rights of individuals, ensuring that information is collected and processed fairly.&lt;SEP&gt;Data protection law encompasses the regulations and practices designed to protect individuals' personal data from misuse, mandating how data can be collected and processed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1b92a727425c41637e16da3cb9ac9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ef4cc90d0e3e23ebc122fef44151a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935971</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Historical Data">
      <data key="d0">Historical Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Historical data is data collected in the past, which can sometimes introduce biases if it reflects existing societal inequalities or outdated norms.&lt;SEP&gt;Historical data is past information used in data sets for AI training, which may carry biases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934740</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Governance">
      <data key="d0">Data Governance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data governance encompasses the management of data availability, usability, integrity, and security within an organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934740</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Privacy-Preserving Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Privacy-Preserving Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Privacy-preserving techniques are methods used to ensure the protection of personal data in AI system development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934740</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contextual Setting">
      <data key="d0">Contextual Setting</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Contextual setting refers to the broader environment in which AI systems are intended to operate, influencing their design and use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934740</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Behavioral Features">
      <data key="d0">Behavioral Features</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Behavioral features are specific characteristics of users or data that should be included in datasets for effective AI training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
