    <node id="Voluntary Codes of Conduct">
      <data key="d0">Voluntary Codes of Conduct</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Voluntary Codes of Conduct are guidelines adopted by organizations and companies that aim to ensure ethical practices in the application of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Voluntary Codes of Conduct are guidelines aimed at fostering the ethical application of AI technologies, especially those not classified as high-risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Voluntary Codes of Conduct refer to guidelines created by organizations or states to regulate practices and promote ethical standards, particularly in the context of AI usage and development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8462fb6c49f462e0c2199ce80842ebde</data>
