      <data key="d5">1783935704</data>
    </node>
    <node id="administrative fines">
      <data key="d0">administrative fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fines are penalties imposed for non-compliance with regulatory obligations, with specified amounts stated in Articles 3, 4, and 5.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Fine">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Fine</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An administrative fine refers to a financial penalty imposed for regulatory violations, intended to enforce compliance with established laws and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union or National Law">
      <data key="d0">Union or National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union or national law refers to a set of legal standards and regulations that govern the operation of providers of high-risk AI systems, particularly concerning data protection and governance.&lt;SEP&gt;Union or national law refers to the collective body of laws governing member states, which may include regulations and oversight of administrative fines.&lt;SEP&gt;Union or national law refers to the legal frameworks that regulate the acquisition and use of data, particularly in relation to data protection and AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical and Organisational Measures">
      <data key="d0">Technical and Organisational Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical and organisational measures are the safeguards that must be implemented by deployers to ensure the compliance and safety of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical and organisational measures refer to the practices and systems implemented by operators to ensure compliance with regulations and mitigate infringements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3</data>
