    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2019/2144">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2019/2144</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2019/2144 is a comprehensive legal framework that establishes type-approval requirements for motor vehicles within the European Union, with a strong emphasis on the safety and protection of both occupants and road users. This regulation specifically governs the oversight of high-risk artificial intelligence systems utilized in vehicles, ensuring that such technologies meet robust safety standards. Additionally, Regulation (EU) 2019/2144 is impacted by updates from Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, which enhances its guidelines and requirements. The regulation outlines detailed rules for the type approval and market surveillance of motor vehicles, reinforcing the importance of regulatory compliance and effective governance for vehicle safety in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af15b193dbeb2497919d2971657871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be3ac2351d8798fda8093d05f96f97fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936225</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 300/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 300/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 300/2008 establishes common rules for civil aviation security within the European Union, focusing on comprehensive security measures for civil aviation operations. It is a critical regulation in the aviation sector, addressing both general security protocols and specifications for security equipment relevant to aviation safety. This regulation is positioned within a broader context of regulations pertaining to high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems, highlighting its importance in the modern landscape of technology and safety. Additionally, Regulation (EC) No 300/2008 has been amended by Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, updating its provisions to enhance aviation security in response to evolving challenges. It repeals previous regulations, thereby streamlining the framework for civil aviation security within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936220</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 167/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 167/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 is a legal instrument adopted by the European Union that governs the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles. This regulation includes specific provisions for type approval, which are essential for ensuring that these vehicles meet established safety and performance standards. It has been amended by Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, enhancing its framework and provisions.

Additionally, Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 also addresses aspects related to artificial intelligence systems embedded in agricultural machinery. This connection highlights the regulation's role in overseeing not just traditional vehicle safety and compliance, but also the implications of advanced technologies such as AI within the agricultural sector. Thus, Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 serves as a crucial regulatory foundation for the development, approval, and market oversight of modern agricultural and forestry vehicles in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 168/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 168/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 addresses the approval and market surveillance of two- or three-wheel vehicles and quadricycles, relevant for AI technologies in transportation.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 concerns the type-approval of two or three-wheel vehicles, relevant for safety concerns associated with AI components in vehicles.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 is a piece of legislation concerning safety components of Artificial Intelligence systems adopted by the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 pertains to the approval and market surveillance of two- or three-wheel vehicles and quadricycles within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 establishes rules on the type approval of two- or three-wheel vehicles and is one of the regulations amended by Regulation 2024/1689.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2018/858">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2018/858</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2018/858 is a comprehensive legislative framework established by the European Union that sets forth requirements for the type approval of motor vehicles, trailers, and their components. The regulation emphasizes the importance of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems integrated within these vehicles, ensuring that such technologies meet stringent safety and performance standards. It governs both the approval process and market surveillance for motor vehicles and their parts across the EU, thereby reinforcing regulatory compliance and consumer protection.

Furthermore, Regulation (EU) 2018/858 is periodically updated, as seen with the subsequent Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, which reflects ongoing advancements and challenges in automotive technology. The regulation also highlights the EU's commitment to adopting delegated acts concerning AI systems within the automotive sector, thereby ensuring that emerging technologies are effectively managed and regulated. This collaborative and rigorous oversight aims to uphold safety, efficiency, and innovation in the automotive industry.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af15b193dbeb2497919d2971657871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936217</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2018/1139">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2018/1139</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 establishes common aviation safety rules and creates the European Union Aviation Safety Agency. It lays down comprehensive guidelines in civil aviation, amending several previous regulations to enhance safety measures. This regulation is particularly relevant in the context of artificial intelligence (AI) systems utilized in aviation, as it sets out specific safety rules pertaining to the integration and implications of AI in aviation safety components. Furthermore, Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 is referenced within the framework of AI regulation, particularly in Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, and serves as a legislative act that delineates provisions for safety components in AI systems within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 sets the European Union's agency for aviation safety and aspects related to aviation safety regulations being revised in the context of AI as per Regulation 2024/1689.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af15b193dbeb2497919d2971657871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2014/90/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2014/90/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2014/90/EU is a significant piece of legislation that addresses standards for marine equipment and repeals earlier marine equipment directives. This directive not only focuses on ensuring maritime safety through regulatory measures but also extends its implications to emerging technologies, particularly artificial intelligence (AI) applications utilized in maritime contexts. It serves as a regulatory framework that encompasses both the specific equipment used at sea and the compliance requirements for AI systems within the maritime industry. Additionally, Directive 2014/90/EU is linked to ongoing amendments under Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, highlighting its relevance in the evolving landscape of maritime regulations and safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936228</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2016/797">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2016/797</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2016/797 refers to the interoperability of the European railway system and is subject to amendments under Regulation 2024/1689.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2016/797 relates to the interoperability of the railway system within the European Union, relevant to AI in transportation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936228</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2020/1828">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2020/1828</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2020/1828 deals with representative actions for the protection of the collective interests of consumers, linked to AI consumer safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2020/1828 sets regulations for consumer protection in the context of online platforms and is amended alongside the AI rules in Regulation 2024/1689.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936228</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1689/oj">
      <data key="d0">1689/oj</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">1689/oj is a specific category or identifier possibly related to documents, indices, or organizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3440467bfb3879bf5e30fbb107e28162</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934835</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Free and Open-Source Tools">
      <data key="d0">Free and Open-Source Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Free and open-source tools are software and components made available to the public under licenses that allow for unrestricted use and modification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Components">
      <data key="d0">AI Components</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI components denotes specific elements utilized in developing artificial intelligence systems, distinct from general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;AI components refer to software and data used in artificial intelligence systems, including models and tools, which can be provided freely through open-source channels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef570a9dfbda3c55d0d5bcc36fd77c5</data>
