      <data key="d5">1783935069</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Developers">
      <data key="d0">Developers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Developers are individuals or organizations that create software, tools, or services, particularly in the realm of AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation Practices">
      <data key="d0">Documentation Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation practices refer to standards and guidelines, such as model cards and data sheets, aimed at providing clarity and governance in AI development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trustworthy AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Trustworthy AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trustworthy AI systems are those designed with ethical considerations, transparency, and reliability in mind to build user confidence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Deployers of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are organizations or entities responsible for managing high-risk AI systems and ensuring compliance with regulations to protect rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers of high-risk AI systems are organizations or entities responsible for ensuring compliance and monitoring the usage of these systems according to specified guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936025</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Market Surveillance Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant Market Surveillance Authorities oversee the deployment of AI systems to ensure compliance and safety standards are met.&lt;SEP&gt;Relevant market surveillance authorities are regulators that must be informed by deployers of high-risk AI systems in case of identified risks or incidents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Log Data">
      <data key="d0">Log Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Log Data refers to the records generated automatically by AI systems, which must be maintained for compliance purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934873</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulation on AI">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulation on AI</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Regulation on AI outlines the legal framework governing the deployment, monitoring, and operation of AI systems within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Regulation on AI is a legal framework designed to oversee the development and deployment of AI technologies across Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935917</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 49">
      <data key="d0">Article 49</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 49 outlines registration obligations for public authorities and Union institutions using high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 49 outlines the procedural aspects and responsibilities related to the registration and updating of AI systems in the EU database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-remote biometric identification system">
      <data key="d0">Post-remote biometric identification system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A post-remote biometric identification system is a technology for identifying individuals remotely, typically for law enforcement or security purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Workers Representatives">
      <data key="d0">Workers Representatives</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Workers’ Representatives are individuals or groups designated to represent the interests and rights of workers, particularly during the implementation of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Affected Workers">
      <data key="d0">Affected Workers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Affected Workers are employees who will be directly impacted by the usage of high-risk AI systems in their workplace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Authority">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative Authority is the government body responsible for making decisions regarding the regulation and enforcement of laws concerning high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Impact Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Impact Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Data Protection Impact Assessment is a process to evaluate how a high-risk AI system may affect the privacy of individuals and ensure compliance with data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Protection Impact Assessments are required evaluations under EU regulation to identify risks to personal data rights.&lt;SEP&gt;The Data Protection Impact Assessment is a process designed to evaluate how data protection rights are impacted by various technologies and practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f4621c3d73dca675e991da5d0c9317</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Remote Biometric Identification System">
      <data key="d0">Post-Remote Biometric Identification System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-Remote Biometric Identification Systems are advanced technology solutions designed for identifying individuals based on biometric data, subject to strict regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supervisory Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Supervisory Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Supervisory Authorities are independent public authorities responsible for monitoring compliance with data protection laws and ensuring individuals' rights are upheld in relation to personal data processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers of high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">Deployers of high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers must consult with Workers’ Representatives to inform about the deployment of high-risk AI systems in the workplace.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="World Trade Organization">
      <data key="d0">World Trade Organization</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The World Trade Organization is an international organization that governs trade agreements and agreements on technical barriers to trade among member countries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_127.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Bodies are entities that perform evaluations to determine whether a product, service, or system meets applicable standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Bodies are organizations that assess whether systems, particularly AI systems, meet specified standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment bodies are organizations authorized to assess compliance with regulatory standards, crucial for mutual recognition agreements.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment bodies are organizations responsible for evaluating the compliance of products and services with regulations, established under laws of various countries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_127.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="World Trade Organization Agreement on Technical Barriers to Trade">
      <data key="d0">World Trade Organization Agreement on Technical Barriers to Trade</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The World Trade Organization Agreement on Technical Barriers to Trade facilitates international trade by establishing guidelines for the recognition of conformity assessments between member countries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_127.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Territory">
      <data key="d0">Territory</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Territory refers to the geographical areas where conformity assessment bodies are established and operate, impacting the mutual recognition agreements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_127.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Country">
      <data key="d0">Third Country</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A third country in this context refers to any country that is not a member of the Union or the World Trade Organization, relevant for mutual recognition discussions.&lt;SEP&gt;A third country refers to any nation that is not a member of the Union but may have agreements with the Union regarding the activities of conformity assessment bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;A third country refers to a nation that is not part of the European Union and may engage in cooperation or agreements regarding law enforcement and judicial matters with the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_127.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935856</data>
    </node>
    <node id="undertakings">
      <data key="d0">undertakings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Undertakings denote businesses or organizations engaged in economic activity, which are also protected under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934882</data>
    </node>
    <node id="innovation">
      <data key="d0">innovation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Innovation refers to the development and implementation of new ideas, processes, or technologies that the Union aims to support and promote.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934882</data>
    </node>
    <node id="employment">
      <data key="d0">employment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Employment indicates the creation of job opportunities and workforce engagement that the Union seeks to enhance through its policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934882</data>
    </node>
    <node id="trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trustworthy AI refers to artificial intelligence systems that adhere to ethical standards, transparency, and user safety, which the Union aims to lead in developing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934882</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Education">
      <data key="d0">Education</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Education encompasses the processes of acquiring and sharing knowledge and skills, essential for participation in the economy and society.&lt;SEP&gt;Education is a context where AI systems targeting emotional detection could lead to discrimination and unfavorable treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Education is a public interest area where services are provided for societal benefit and often intersects with technology deployments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7df88d0d68bb9e14cc05c3f581da8399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936168</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Reasons">
      <data key="d0">Medical Reasons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical reasons refer to justifiable contexts where AI systems may be employed without the same concerns as in workplace or educational situations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Therapeutical Use">
      <data key="d0">Therapeutical Use</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Therapeutical use encompasses applications of AI systems that cater to medical needs and do not pose the same ethical dilemmas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discriminatory Outcomes">
      <data key="d0">Discriminatory Outcomes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discriminatory outcomes refer to unfair treatment of specific individuals or groups resulting from AI system assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intrusiveness">
      <data key="d0">Intrusiveness</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intrusiveness refers to the intrusive nature of AI systems that can violate the rights and freedoms of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Prohibition">
      <data key="d0">Market Prohibition</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market prohibition relates to regulations preventing the sale or use of certain AI systems in sensitive contexts like workplaces and education.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Affected Person">
      <data key="d0">Affected Person</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Affected persons are individuals subject to decisions made by AI systems that critically impact them, and they are entitled to explanations regarding these decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_86.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934896</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Law Exceptions">
      <data key="d0">Union Law Exceptions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law exceptions refer to specific conditions under which certain obligations regarding AI systems may be limited or restricted based on national laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_86.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934900</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Performance of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance of AI Systems refers to the operational efficiency and functionality of AI systems, especially those that continue to learn and adapt post-market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_128.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934906</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operating System">
      <data key="d0">Operating System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An Operating System is the software that supports a computer's basic functions and may need evaluation when changes affect AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_128.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783934906</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Software Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Software Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Software Architecture refers to the fundamental structures of a software system and is crucial to assess if modified in high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_128.json</data>
