    <node id="Codes of Conduct">
      <data key="d0">Codes of Conduct</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Codes of conduct are formalized guidelines established by organizations or stakeholders to ensure ethical and appropriate behavior in the deployment of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Codes of conduct serve as guidelines for the voluntary application of ethical standards in the development and use of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Codes of conduct are guidelines that providers of AI systems can voluntarily adopt to ensure ethical and responsible development and deployment of their technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc</data>
