    <node id="Publicly Accessible Spaces">
      <data key="d0">Publicly Accessible Spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly Accessible Spaces refer to areas that are open to the public where AI systems may be deployed for biometric identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are areas that are open for anyone to enter, defined against the criteria of prohibitive signs or restrictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces refer to locations where individuals can gather or pass through without specific restrictions, often serving as environments for the deployment of biometric identification technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are locations where individuals can be present without restrictions, making them potential sites for surveillance and biometric identification.</data>
