    <node id="Third Countries">
      <data key="d0">Third Countries</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Third Countries are nations that are not part of the European Union but may enter into agreements or cooperation frameworks with the EU for law enforcement and judicial purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Third Countries are nations that are not part of the European Union but may interact with EU regulatory frameworks, especially concerning AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Third countries refer to nations outside the European Union that may receive data transfers, subject to specific safeguards according to EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88</data>
