      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The five-year period refers to the duration granted to the Commission for the delegation of powers, starting from 1 August 2024.&lt;SEP&gt;The five-year period refers to the time frame during which documents related to the assessment of subcontractors must be retained.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subcontractor">
      <data key="d0">Subcontractor</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8</data>
      <data key="d2">A notified body is responsible for ensuring that subcontractors meet the necessary standards for conformity assessment tasks.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935403</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subsidiary">
      <data key="d0">Subsidiary</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8</data>
      <data key="d2">Notified bodies oversee the operations of their subsidiaries, ensuring they adhere to regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935403</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 71">
      <data key="d0">Article 71</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 71 refers to a specific legal provision in EU law which mandates the secure handling of certain data within the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 specifies the requirements for the registration and use of high-risk AI systems in the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 refers to the functioning of the EU database as it relates to regulatory compliance and evaluation of AI within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783936104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 6(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 6(3) defines the criteria for determining whether an AI system is classified as high-risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 6(3) identifies AI systems that are not considered high-risk, providing criteria for their classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 6(3) refers to the specific regulation defining the classification criteria for high-risk AI systems that must be evaluated by authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bodies, Offices, and Agencies">
      <data key="d0">Bodies, Offices, and Agencies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">These refer to various entities operating under the EU framework that have specific roles, including the enforcement of regulations related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935418</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 74(8)">
      <data key="d0">Article 74(8)</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 74(8) specifies the access rights regarding the restricted sections of the EU database for the Commission and national authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935418</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex IX">
      <data key="d0">Annex IX</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex IX contains additional guidelines and points relevant to the registration process and management of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IX outlines further protocols for information and access procedures within the regulations of the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IX specifies information that must be included in the registration of AI systems and real-world testing plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935794</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 74">
      <data key="d0">Article 74</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 74 details access regulations for specific sections of the EU database that are limited to the Commission and national authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 74 outlines specific provisions related to market surveillance authority in the context of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935556</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Product">
      <data key="d0">Product</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A product is defined as any item that is placed on the market or put into service, which can include equipment and systems that may have high-risk AI components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations of the Provider">
      <data key="d0">Obligations of the Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations of the provider refer to the responsibilities defined under regulations that manufacturers and service providers must fulfill for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783935419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Panel">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Panel</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Scientific Panel is a collective of experts that assists in developing standards and practices regarding AI models, providing knowledge and guidance in the process.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel is tasked with assessing the compliance of AI models and can request information from providers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel provides qualified alerts and assessments related to AI capabilities, influencing Commission decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0</data>
