    <edge source="Commission" target="Regulation (EU) No 182/2011">
      <data key="d6">28.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 pertains to the powers exercised by the Commission and requires control mechanisms by Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is governed by Regulation (EU) No 182/2011, which outlines how its implementing powers are to be controlled by Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is guided by the stipulations of Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 regarding the functions and assistance of committees.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,implementation authority,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3fa5fe9ac042448be58de6c82bb33ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37c30ee0e0a87b8ea9630ea20f092fa</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_98.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_175.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934173</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="Committee">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission is assisted by the Committee as per the provisions of Regulation (EU) No 182/2011.</data>
      <data key="d8">delegation,governance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e37c30ee0e0a87b8ea9630ea20f092fa</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_98.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934103</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="law enforcement authority">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Law enforcement authorities may be subject to regulations set by the Commission concerning the use of AI and biometric systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">law enforcement,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934170</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">120.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office and the Commission maintain a collaborative relationship focused on the governance, implementation, and standardization of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Operating under the jurisdiction of the Commission, the AI Office plays a crucial role in initiating requests for guideline updates, which fosters interaction between the two entities. This partnership allows for structured discussions regarding AI models, their associated risks, and the necessary measures to align these with the Commission's oversight.

The Commission is responsible for guiding the AI Office in addressing identified risks related to AI technologies while also evaluating the AI Office's operational effectiveness in enforcing AI regulations. In this capacity, the Commission empowers the AI Office to monitor AI models for systemic risks, reflecting the regulatory authority it possesses over the classification of these models. Furthermore, the AI Office develops methodologies that assist the Commission in reviewing and assessing AI regulations and practices.

Overall, this collaborative framework emphasizes the Commission's pivotal role in regulating the AI Office, aiming to enhance the governance and safety of AI implementations through the establishment of regulations and procedures related to the access, evaluation, and compliance of AI models. Together, they strive to uphold obligations concerning AI standards and ensure a systematic approach to mitigating risks associated with AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office collaborates with the Commission to ensure compliance of AI model providers through structured dialogues.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission empowers the AI Office to monitor and control the implementation of AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission may rely on input from the AI Office to decide on the adequacy of codes of practice for AI compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office works alongside the Commission to develop and implement codes of practice related to AI content obligations.</data>
      <data key="d8">authority,collaboration,compliance oversight,evaluation,governance,initiative request,inter-organizational collaboration,methodology development,monitoring authority,organizational function,oversight,policy implementation,regulation,regulatory authority,regulatory collaboration,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,regulatory function,regulatory oversight,regulatory relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
