    <edge source="Commission" target="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d6">59.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission and the Market Surveillance Authority have a structured and interdependent relationship defined by directives, oversight, and accountability. The Commission issues directives and decisions that the Market Surveillance Authority is mandated to enforce, particularly concerning authorizations and compliance assessments. In its role, the Commission oversees the activities of the Market Surveillance Authorities, ensuring that they operate in alignment with EU regulations and guidelines.

Moreover, the Commission provides essential guidance and oversight to the Market Surveillance Authority, specifically in enforcing regulations pertaining to artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This includes a requirement for the Market Surveillance Authority to inform the Commission about any authorizations related to high-risk AI systems, thereby reinforcing a system of accountability between the two entities. The Market Surveillance Authority must regularly report its findings and activities to the Commission, reflecting a clear framework of regulatory oversight in which the Commission outlines the regulatory frameworks that the Market Surveillance Authority adheres to in its operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority must inform the Commission about the evaluation results of AI systems that may have cross-border implications.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU governance,compliance,governance,information sharing,oversight,regulatory authority,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement,regulatory guidance,regulatory oversight,regulatory process</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783935741</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="Board">
      <data key="d6">46.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Board and the Commission work in close collaboration to enhance the framework for Artificial Intelligence (AI) regulation. Together, they provide comprehensive advice and support for the implementation of these regulations, focusing particularly on small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and startups. The Commission plays a vital role in supporting the Board's activities, especially in establishing groups tasked with market surveillance to ensure adherence to the regulatory framework.

In their joint efforts, the Board offers guidance and facilitates coordination among national authorities to promote effective AI regulations. The Commission, in turn, consults with the Board to ensure that proper guidelines are developed for AI systems, making sure that both entities are aligned in their objectives. Overall, their collaboration aims to enhance resources and support for SMEs, ensuring that they can effectively navigate compliance in the evolving landscape of AI regulation.</data>
      <data key="d8">7,advisory role,collaboration,coordination,guidance,regulatory framework,regulatory support,resource enhancement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacbea1ddddc58fbf14c882b36d9a6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16</data>
