    <edge source="Commission" target="Member State">
      <data key="d6">55.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission consults experts from each Member State before adopting delegated acts, highlighting the involvement of Member States in the legislative procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission plays a critical role in overseeing the compliance of Member States with EU regulations and common specifications. Member States are required to inform the Commission to confirm that they adhere to these standards and regulation requirements. This involves notifying the Commission about their national rules as outlined in the Regulation, which indicates a compliance relationship between the two entities. Additionally, Member States must report any administrative fines they have issued to the Commission on an annual basis. In matters of authorizations and regulatory issues, the Commission directly addresses decisions to the relevant Member State. Furthermore, the Commission evaluates the measures taken by Member States concerning AI practices to ensure they align with EU laws, reinforcing its mandate to oversee compliance across the Union.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,consultation,decision-making,governance,member state involvement,oversight,regulatory authority,regulatory compliance,regulatory oversight,reporting obligation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e</data>
