    <edge source="Commission" target="Regulation">
      <data key="d6">65.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission is responsible for approving codes of practice under the Regulation and ensuring adherence to compliance obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission plays a crucial role in enforcing and developing guidelines according to the requirements established in the Regulation. It is responsible for implementing and assessing the Regulation related to AI practices, ensuring compliance among Member States, and proposing amendments when necessary. Furthermore, the Commission oversees the application of the Regulation that governs Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) and is tasked with ensuring that these entities adhere to established compliance frameworks. Through its regulatory oversight, the Commission ensures that Member States comply with the guidelines set forth in the Regulation. In summary, the Commission is integral to the drafting, enforcement, and assessment of regulations that govern AI practices and SMEs within the European Union, ensuring adherence and promoting necessary updates to the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">10,compliance,compliance oversight,enforcement,governance,oversight,regulatory assessment,regulatory authority,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight,regulatory role</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e4f07f79ad3c90c82b86c0a02d0fae9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0</data>
