    <edge source="European Parliament" target="Regulation (EU) 2024/1689">
      <data key="d6">98.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Parliament plays a pivotal role in the legislative process surrounding Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, which governs artificial intelligence (AI) safety and standards within the European Union. This regulation lays down specific rules for AI systems, and the European Parliament is tasked with drafting, discussing, and ultimately adopting it. Through its legislative responsibilities, the Parliament oversees and modifies the regulation to ensure it effectively addresses safety components in AI systems.

As the primary legislative body, the European Parliament significantly influences the legal framework of artificial intelligence and its applications. By developing and approving Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the Parliament contributes critically to policy-making in the field of AI, underscoring its importance in shaping the regulatory landscape for this emerging technology. Overall, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 exemplifies the European Parliament's commitment to governing AI, emphasizing its essential role in establishing safety standards and enhancing regulatory practices.</data>
      <data key="d8">9,governance,legislation,legislative authority,legislative oversight,legislative process,legislative role,policy-making,regulation passage,regulatory development,regulatory framework,regulatory governance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4219a2a10d85ddd82f98b8d6267cb9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783936232</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Parliament" target="Council of the European Union">
      <data key="d6">86.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The European Parliament and the Council of the European Union work together in the legislative process, including the approval of directives like the one discussed."\&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union and the European Parliament collaborate closely in the legislative process of the European Union (EU). Together, they are responsible for establishing important regulations, including those that govern cybersecurity requirements for products with digital elements and the framework for high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This partnership reflects the dual legislative process inherent in the EU's structure, ensuring balanced decision-making and participation by both institutions.

The European Parliament and the Council work in concert not only to create and pass EU legislation but also to amend existing regulations such as the Digital Services Act. Their joint efforts influence policy decisions across various sectors, highlighting their significant role in shaping EU law and governance. Through this collaborative approach, they strive to address emerging challenges and promote effective regulatory frameworks within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Both the European Parliament and the Council of the European Union participate in creating and enacting regulations regarding high-risk AI systems in the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union collaborates with the European Parliament on legislative matters affecting member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament and the Council of the European Union work together on legislation and policies, shaping the legal framework of the EU.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU governance,collaboration,governance,joint governance,joint regulation,law-making,legislation,legislative approval,legislative collaboration,legislative partnership,legislative process,policy making</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74def3a33d9c60f3c11227adf7704a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdc616126c9eed60b2893f6f0c5a24b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa5fe9ac042448be58de6c82bb33ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb00b9eef4af47cdd3264cd99d6b2e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a48f68b8943ab2f8e6bdbb9ccf3e17d</data>
