      <data key="d11">1783934132</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union" target="National Level">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Union works alongside national authorities to ensure compliance with the Regulation at the country-specific level.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_167.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934134</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union" target="Regulation">
      <data key="d6">66.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation is a key component of the legislative framework established by the Union to manage AI technologies effectively. It serves as a legislative act enforced within the Union, outlining the compliance requirements for AI systems. The Regulation emphasizes the importance of confidentiality and security for all parties involved within the Union's legal framework, thus ensuring that AI systems are handled responsibly and ethically.

Additionally, the Union creates regulations that are applicable to its institutions in relation to various activities, including the deployment of AI systems. This comprehensive approach enables the Union to maintain a level playing field in the AI sector, ensuring that all operators, both within and outside its borders, comply with the established standards. By enacting the Regulation, the Union seeks to govern AI systems within its jurisdiction, ensuring that they align with its legal frameworks and uphold the values of safety and accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation is a legal measure that the Union may adopt to better address issues related to AI and market functioning than individual Member States could achieve on their own.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU compliance,EU legislation,compliance,enforcement,governance,internal market,legal guidelines,legislative framework,policy creation,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ba08954f9ed754c2566e3c59b63ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714d9f621f6eee9273625419653b083c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934985</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union" target="Notifying Authority">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Union establishes the framework within which the Notifying Authority operates to ensure regulatory compliance for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance oversight,regulatory governance</data>
