    <edge source="AI Systems" target="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">58.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI Systems encompass a broad category of technologies that can significantly impact individuals' rights and lives. Among these, certain AI Systems are classified as High-Risk due to their intended purpose and potential to cause harm. High-Risk AI Systems are subject to specific criteria outlined under EU regulations, which necessitate stricter enforcement and compliance requirements. Notably, AI Systems that determine eligibility for services are categorized as High-Risk because of their significant impact on individuals. Additionally, AI Systems used in education may also fall under the High-Risk classification when they affect access and evaluation, thereby influencing individuals' lives substantially. While not all AI Systems are deemed High-Risk, those that are face more rigorous regulatory scrutiny to mitigate their potential risks.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are a specific category within the broader framework of AI systems that require stricter regulation due to their potential impact.</data>
      <data key="d8">category classification,classification,educational impact,oversight,regulatory compliance,regulatory context,regulatory distinction,risk assessment,risk classification,risk management,technology assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7df88d0d68bb9e14cc05c3f581da8399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4</data>
