      <data key="d11">1783934332</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="SMEs">
      <data key="d6">29.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are tasked with supporting SMEs through initiatives targeted specifically at their needs to promote innovation in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States must consider the specific interests and needs of SMEs when setting conformity assessment fees.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States must ensure that SMEs are properly supported in understanding and complying with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States consider the specific interests and needs of SMEs when developing AI governance frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d8">business support,financial consideration,regulation,regulatory compliance,regulatory consideration,regulatory obligations,support,support measures</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934909</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">48.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office and Member States engage in a collaborative partnership aimed at enhancing AI capabilities and ensuring compliance with relevant regulations. Member States are tasked with facilitating the operations of the AI Office, which includes implementing the penalties and rules set forth by the Regulation. The AI Office works closely with Member States to develop actions that promote adherence to these regulations, including the establishment of ethical guidelines and codes of conduct for AI systems. Additionally, the AI Office provides assistance to Member States in the implementation of AI regulations and in enhancing their technical expertise. Through this collaboration, both entities strive to foster a responsible and effective AI environment.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,cooperation,governance,implementation support,regulation collaboration,regulatory compliance,regulatory implementation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783936118</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="Conformity Assessment Body">
      <data key="d6">13.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Conformity assessment bodies must maintain regular compliance and documentation checks as required by the Member States and the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States interact with the Conformity Assessment Body to ensure adherence to the standards that the Commission addresses.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance monitoring,regulatory adherence,regulatory obligations</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934306</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="The Commission">
      <data key="d6">15.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States collaborate with The Commission on the enforcement and supervision of Chapter V under the Treaties.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission consults with Member States to address objections and decide on authorisation matters.</data>
      <data key="d8">cooperation,governance,regulatory consultation,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783935756</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="Standardisation Development Processes">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States facilitate the participation of SMEs in Standardisation Development Processes to ensure comprehensive regulations are developed.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934335</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="Public Authorities">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States function as public authorities responsible for regulating AI systems and supporting SMEs and start-ups in their compliance efforts.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783934335</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="Regulation">
      <data key="d6">68.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are fundamental in the application and enforcement of the Regulation, ensuring its implementation within their jurisdictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States are required to comply with and enforce the standards, penalties, and provisions outlined in the Regulation related to artificial intelligence (AI) practices. They hold the responsibility of establishing regulations governing the use and deployment of AI systems, particularly focusing on small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and start-ups. Furthermore, Member States must specifically adhere to the Regulation concerning high-risk AI systems and enforce its provisions to ensure consumer protection. It is essential for Member States to implement the Regulation within their jurisdictions effectively to guarantee compliance and to ensure the proper enforcement of associated penalties.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States are required to adhere to and implement the guidelines set forth in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d8">collective action,compliance,enforcement,governance,implementation,legislative obligation,regulation,regulation adherence,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_69.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783936177</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d6">32.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Each member state has national competent authorities responsible for the enforcement of regulations and the administration of fines.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States are required to designate national competent authorities and ensure they are adequately resourced.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States are responsible for establishing National Competent Authorities that oversee AI regulations and enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States designate National Competent Authorities to supervise the application of regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">authority designation,enforcement,governance,implementation,regulation oversight,regulatory framework,regulatory responsibility,resource allocation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783935568</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d6">24.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States appoint Market Surveillance Authorities to enforce and monitor compliance with the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States can designate a Market Surveillance Authority to ensure compliance with EU regulations."|"regulatory authority, compliance regulation&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority's authorizations must be communicated to Member States, implicating their cooperation in regulatory actions.</data>
      <data key="d8">8,collaboration,monitoring compliance,regulatory oversight,regulatory responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783935568</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Member States" target="AI Solutions">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are encouraged to promote the development of AI Solutions aimed at achieving socially beneficial results.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI development,international cooperation</data>
