    <edge source="Member States" target="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d6">48.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market Surveillance Authorities operate within Member States to enforce European Union (EU) regulations and conduct market surveillance efforts effectively. Member States facilitate coordination between these authorities to enhance compliance with Union law. They are responsible for appointing and designating Market Surveillance Authorities to ensure that compliance measures are upheld, particularly concerning high-risk AI systems. Furthermore, Member States manage and oversee the activities of these authorities in relation to market-specific regulations, as stipulated by Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, thereby ensuring that there is rigorous oversight and incident reporting related to AI systems as required by EU regulations.</data>
