    <edge source="Regulation" target="National Law">
      <data key="d6">55.0</data>
      <data key="d7">National law may provide exceptions or restrictions to the application of regulations concerning AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Law is designed to be consistent with the Regulation, ensuring that the tasks performed by authorities align with the regulatory framework. It establishes the foundational legal framework for conformity assessment, thereby providing the necessary support for the implementation of the Regulation. The Regulation acts as a superior legal framework that mandates Member States to align their National Law when considering the authorization of specific uses. Furthermore, the National Law serves to implement the Regulation and its requirements for authorization, thereby facilitating compliance. Additionally, the Regulation delineates the interaction between its provisions and national laws, particularly concerning law enforcement authorizations. Lastly, regulations established under Union law impose limits and standards that must be adhered to within the National Law, especially regarding the use of personal data.</data>
