      <data key="d11">1783934226</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">81.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office is an entity responsible for developing standardized templates and a platform in relation to the Regulation concerning artificial intelligence. It undertakes various actions as mandated by the Regulation to manage and regulate AI systems throughout the Union. Operating under the framework of the Regulation, the AI Office facilitates compliance and addresses systemic risks associated with AI usage. Its primary tasks include ensuring the effective implementation and adherence to the provisions of the Regulation related to AI, particularly focusing on general-purpose AI models. Moreover, the AI Office is tasked with monitoring and enforcing the Regulation, ensuring compliance and providing oversight in the AI sector.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office's role is to evaluate codes and standards within the context of the Regulation to ensure they meet compliance needs.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office operates under the guidelines set by the Regulation to monitor compliance among AI model providers.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is tasked with enforcing the Regulation by monitoring compliance among AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance evaluation,compliance oversight,compliance support,enforcement,monitoring responsibility,operational guidance,operational mandate,oversight,regulation implementation,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6579442a2f027e643cf907006333003a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18d33fd192f06f727ac6bb21becbaa57</data>
