    <edge source="Regulation" target="European Union">
      <data key="d6">56.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Union is actively involved in the creation and development of regulations to manage the implementation and implications of artificial intelligence (AI) systems across its member states. These regulations aim to ensure safety, compliance, and the governance of high-risk AI systems, establishing a clear legal framework that addresses the activities and requirements of conformity assessment and notified bodies. The Regulation is a key component of this framework, designed to streamline legal processes and govern the use and market of AI systems within the jurisdiction of the European Union. By doing so, the European Union seeks to promote consistency and adherence to standards among its member states regarding AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU legislation,governance,jurisdiction,legal authority,legislative oversight,regulatory authority,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5928be36056ac91865bd3e4d596159e</data>
