    <edge source="AI Office" target="Providers of General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d6">42.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must report relevant information about serious incidents to the AI Office as part of their regulatory obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office oversees compliance and regulatory reporting from providers of general-purpose AI models regarding systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office invites providers of general-purpose AI models to participate in the drawing up of codes of practice.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office invites these providers to adhere to specific codes of practice concerning AI model usage and risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office encourages participation from providers of general-purpose AI models when developing codes of practice.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,industry standards,oversight,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,regulatory input,stakeholder engagement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0</data>
