    <edge source="Provider" target="High-Risk AI System">
      <data key="d6">63.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Provider of a High-Risk AI System is tasked with several critical responsibilities under the applicable regulations. They are primarily accountable for complying with safety requirements as outlined in Section 2 of the regulation. This includes the obligation to ensure that the high-risk AI systems they develop meet EU regulations and technical compliance standards. Additionally, the Provider must manage and ensure compliance not only during the initial development of these systems but also after any modifications are made. By placing high-risk AI systems on the market, the Provider underscores its commitment to uphold all related obligations, ensuring that the systems adhere to established safety and compliance protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is responsible for the placement and service of high-risk AI systems, ensuring compliance with legal requirements.</data>
      <data key="d8">accountability,compliance,compliance assurance,creation,development,obligation,regulatory compliance,regulatory responsibility,responsibility,risk management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19283d37b8085eb0b86aff77d85558de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
